[stderr] +sequence: 8
[stderr] +title: Dispatch the next bounded implementation-runbook authoring wave
[stderr] +browser_impact: not_applicable
[stderr] +playwright_spec:
[stderr] +---
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Objective
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Run one durable authoring-dispatch iteration after the bootstrap B0001–B0006
[stderr] +wave. First expand at most one eligible queued specification/catalogue chapter
[stderr] +into no more than 250 `IMP-*` records and validate its requirement/dependency
[stderr] +coverage. Then allocate ready, unassigned contracts into at most ten new
[stderr] +B-series authoring tasks, each with at most seven R-series outputs. Create
[stderr] +exactly one successor dispatcher when a queued chapter or ready contract
[stderr] +remains; create the final audit B-series task instead only when neither exists.
[stderr] +Exit after creating that bounded set.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Context packet
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Read `INITIAL.md`, `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `../specification/README.md`,
[stderr] +`../planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json`,
[stderr] +`../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`, its Markdown ledger, and
[stderr] +`../../../runbooks/F014.md`. Read only the canonical specification sections
[stderr] +needed for the one selected chapter. Treat SHARD-05 as held unless explicit
[stderr] +authorisation is recorded; do not turn a gate into approval.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Required behaviour
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Select no more than one queued chapter whose dependencies and gates permit
[stderr] +planning. Add at most 250 stable `IMP-*` contracts with requirement links,
[stderr] +owned files/data/interfaces, dependencies, non-goals, platform distinctions,
[stderr] +verification, asset assessment, and canonical source links. Validate coverage,
[stderr] +unique IDs, ownership, and acyclic dependencies. Allocate only ready
[stderr] +unassigned contracts, using monotonic B/R counters and batches of no more than
[stderr] +seven R IDs; materialise at most ten corresponding B runbooks. Each B writer
[stderr] +must contain a context packet, output list, validation procedure,
[stderr] +checkpoint/update procedure, collision stop rule, and stop condition. Do not
[stderr] +create R-series files yourself.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Checkpoint and update procedure
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Atomically update the JSON/Markdown ledger counters, chapter state, contract
[stderr] +allocations, and checkpoint after validation. Never renumber, replace, or
[stderr] +rewrite an accepted B/R contract. If work remains, create exactly one new
[stderr] +dispatcher with the next monotonic dispatcher ID and a later sequence. If no
[stderr] +queued chapter or ready contract remains, create exactly one final audit
[stderr] +B-series runbook that validates all completed catalogue expansions and batches;
[stderr] +it must not pretend to generate or review all work in this dispatch.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Validation procedure
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Validate JSON, the 250-contract chapter cap, no more than ten newly-created B
[stderr] +files, no more than seven assigned R IDs per B file, unique B/R/IMP IDs,
[stderr] +dependency closure, provenance values, asset metadata, output ownership, and
[stderr] +the successor/final-audit choice. Stop and report a source conflict, missing
[stderr] +coverage, cycle, ID/path collision, unresolved authority, or any need to
[stderr] +overwrite accepted work.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Stop condition
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Stop immediately after one chapter expansion (or none), one allocation wave,
[stderr] +and exactly one successor dispatcher or final audit task. This is not a
[stderr] +recursive prompt and must not materialise a whole-game plan.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Acceptance criteria
