ource-of-truth ownership, and original-art acceptance checks.\nFor `not_applicable`, that section must explain why the scope needs no generated\nor source visual asset and explicitly prohibit incidental asset creation. This\nkeeps UI, illustration, icon, texture, sprite, audio-visual, and other product\nasset work visible in the implementation plan instead of discovering it midway\nthrough coding.\n\nEach B-series authoring task may create at most seven R-series implementation\nrunbooks. It must stop after its assigned seven (or fewer), update the manifest,\nand leave remaining work for the next bounded batch.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- The initial collection contains only a bounded bootstrap wave; each\n  dispatcher expands at most one 250-contract domain shard, creates at most ten\n  new B-series authoring tasks plus one successor, then exits. It never attempts\n  to materialise the whole game plan.\n- There is exactly one valid B-series authoring runbook per allocated manifest\n  batch, and it creates no more than seven assigned R-series runbooks.\n- B-series runbooks never overwrite an existing R-series contract with a\n  conflicting ID; they stop and report mismatches.\n- Every generated B-series runbook includes its context packet, output list,\n  validation procedure, checkpoint/update procedure, and a clear stop condition.\n- Both child-collection registration files exist, contain valid JSON with a\n  relative `runbooks_dir`, and point to the generated authoring and\n  implementation collections respectively.\n- R-series contracts use stable IDs and parse with the Supervisor runbook\n  loader; their declared dependencies match the manifest, every contract has\n  explicit `asset_impact` and `asset_ids` metadata, and asset-required\n  contracts have non-empty stable IDs. Every R contract also has non-empty,\n  valid `source_specifications`, `source_catalogue_ids`, `authoring_batch`,\n  and `factory_stages` provenance metadata.\n- The collection contains a final audit B-series task after all authoring\n  batches and catalogue expansions are complete, rather than pretending that\n  thousands of contracts can be reviewed in one generation step.\n# Runbook-authoring allocation ledger\n\nThis readable companion to [`runbook-authoring-manifest.json`](runbook-authoring-manifest.json) is the persistent allocation ledger for the mock-fantasy-quest-4 authoring system. The JSON is authoritative for IDs, provenance, dependencies, output paths, counters, and recovery state. Accepted IDs are immutable: resume from the first non-accepted batch and append only at `B0007` and `R0013`.\n\n## Wave 1 \u2014 foundation contracts\n\n| Order | Batch | R contracts (maximum 7) | Dependency / parallel disposition | Checkpoint |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | B0001 | R0001 | GATE-0001; no parallel work | Record gate and R0001 ownership |\n| 2 | B0002 | R0002, R0003, R0010 | After B0001 | Validate seams, fixtures, tokens and retained gates |\n| 3 | B0003 | R0004, R0008 | After B0002 | Validate state slice and P0 service exclusion |\n| 4 | B0004 | R0005, R0006 | After B0003; R0006 waits for GATE-0003 | Validate content/save separation |\n| 5 | B0005 | R0007, R0009, R0011 | After B0004; R0007/GATE-0003 and R0009/GATE-0005 remain blocked | Validate migration, diagnostics, provenance |\n| 6 | B0006 | R0012 | After B0003 and B0004; safe in parallel with B0005 after B0004 | Cross-check foundation documentation and gates |\n\nThe batches are deliberately smaller than seven where a contract is context-heavy (state, persistence, content) or tightly coupled to its predecessor. Together they form an incremental foundation vertical slice: reproducible baseline, shared seams/test harness, deterministic game state and P0 exclusion, content and recovery boundaries, then provenance/diagnostic controls and documented closure. They do not imply that the game is implemented.\n\n## Contract allocation and asset assessment\n\n| R ID | IMP source | Writer | Output | Asset assessment |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| R0001 | IMP-0001 | B0001 | `runbooks/R0001.md` | not applicable \u2014 tooling boundary only |\n| R0002 | IMP-0002 | B0002 | `runbooks/R0002.md` | not applicable \u2014 interfaces only |\n| R0003 | IMP-0003 | B0002 | `runbooks/R0003.md` | not applicable \u2014 deterministic fixtures only |\n| R0004 | IMP-0004 | B0003 | `runbooks/R0004.md` | not applicable \u2014 state envelopes only |\n| R0005 | IMP-0005 | B0004 | `runbooks/R0005.md` | not applicable \u2014 schema reserves later asset fields |\n| R0006 | IMP-0006 | B0004 | `runbooks/R0006.md` | not applicable \u2014 save/recovery protocol |\n| R0007 | IMP-0007 | B0005 | `runbooks/R0007.md` | not applicable \u2014 migrations only |\n| R0008 | IMP-0008 | B0003 | `runbooks/R0008.md` | not applicable \u2014 negative service scope |\n| R0009 | IMP-0009 | B0005 | `runbooks/R0009.md` | not applicable \u2014 local diagnostics only |\n| R0010 | IMP-0010 | B0002 | `runbooks/R0010.md` | not applicable \u2014 no final art/fonts/icons |\n| R0011 | IMP-0011 | B0005 | `runbooks/R0011.md` | not applicable \u2014 provenance control only |\n| R0012 | IMP-0012 | B0006 | `runbooks/R0012.md` | not applicable \u2014 documentation only |\n\nNo Wave 1 contract creates a product asset. Each contract still carries an explicit `asset_impact`, empty `asset_ids`, and an asset brief in the JSON; its author must prohibit incidental asset creation. A later asset-required contract must reserve stable product-specific IDs and a brief before assignment.\n\n## Author packet and resume rules\n\nEach B writer receives only the baseline terminology, target constraints, templates, authoring rules, and the named specification/catalogue records in its JSON `context_packet`. Every R record has canonical `source_specifications`, `source_catalogue_ids`, `authoring_batch`, and `factory_stages` provenance. Use [`runbooks/TEMPLATE.md`](../../../runbooks/TEMPLATE.md) plus the F014 metadata and asset requirements.\n\nAt every checkpoint, validate unique B/R IDs, output-path ownership, dependency closure, provenance, the batch maximum, asset assessment, and retained human gates. On failure, retain all assigned IDs, repair the bounded failed output, and resume that same batch. Never regenerate accepted contracts or renumber the ledger.\n\n## Queued expansion chapters\n\n| Chapter | Future allocation point | State |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| SHARD-02 \u2014 Campaign content and domain logic | Wave 2 after GATE-0004 | queued |\n| SHARD-03 \u2014 Session, UI, input, and accessibility | Wave 3 after SHARD-02 and GATE-0002/0003/0004 | queued |\n| SHARD-04 \u2014 PWA delivery, performance, operations, release evidence | Wave 4 after SHARD-02/03 and GATE-0002/0005/0007 | queued |\n| SHARD-05 \u2014 Connected-scope decision package | Only explicit authorisation after GATE-0006; no P0 R allocation | hold |\n\nExpand one queued chapter into catalogue records before allocating its R IDs. This preserves the catalogue\u2019s dependency graph and makes a future thousand-runbook programme resumable without changing accepted work.\n\n## Structural check\n\n```sh\nnode -e 'const m=require(\"./projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\"); const r=m.r_contracts, b=m.batches, ids=a=>new Set(a).size===a.length; if (!ids(r.map(x=>x.id)) || !ids(b.map(x=>x.id)) || r.length!==m.expected_runbook_count || b.some(x=>x.r_contract_ids.length>7) || r.some(x=>!x.source_specifications.length || !x.source_catalogue_ids.length || !x.authoring_batch || !x.factory_stages.length || ![\"required\",\"not_applicable\"].includes(x.asset_impact) || !x.output_path || (x.asset_impact===\"required\" && (!x.asset_ids.length || !x.asset_brief))) ) process.exit(1); console.log(\"runbook authoring ledger structural check passed\")'\n```\n{\n  \"manifest_id\": \"mock-fantasy-quest-4-runbook-authoring-ledger\",\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"purpose\": \"Persistent, append-only allocation ledger for bounded B-series authoring batches and immutable R-series implementation contracts. It allocates the current catalogue only; queued shards remain expansion work.\",\n  \"project_slug\": \"mock-fantasy-quest-4\",\n  \"source_catalogue\": \"planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\",\n  \"expected_runbook_count\": 12,\n  \"id_counters\": {\"next_authoring_batch_id\": \"B0007\", \"next_implementation_runbook_id\": \"R0013\", \"rule\": \"Never reuse, renumber, or replace an accepted B or R ID. Append new allocations using these counters only.\"},\n  \"wave\": {\"number\": 1, \"state\": \"planned\", \"checkpoint_after_each_batch\": true, \"resume_from\": \"first batch whose state is not accepted; validate accepted IDs, paths, and provenance before dispatch\", \"recovery\": \"If a batch fails, retain its IDs, mark it blocked or repairable, repair only its listed output paths, validate its contracts, then resume that same batch. Do not reallocate its R IDs.\"},\n  \"catalogue_disposition\": {\"allocated\": [\"IMP-0001\",\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0003\",\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0005\",\"IMP-0006\",\"IMP-0007\",\"IMP-0008\",\"IMP-0009\",\"IMP-0010\",\"IMP-0011\",\"IMP-0012\"], \"deferred\": [], \"human_gates_retained\": {\"IMP-0001\":\"GATE-0001\", \"IMP-0006\":\"GATE-0003\", \"IMP-0007\":\"GATE-0003\", \"IMP-0009\":\"GATE-0005\", \"IMP-0010\":\"GATE-0002,GATE-0004\"}},\n  \"queued_expansion\": [\n    {\"chapter\":\"SHARD-02\",\"title\":\"Campaign content and domain logic\",\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\"],\"state\":\"queued\",\"future_wave\":\"wave 2 after GATE-0004\",\"allocation_rule\":\"expand into bounded IMP records before assigning any R IDs\"},\n    {\"chapter\":\"SHARD-03\",\"title\":\"Session, UI, input, and accessibility\",\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\",\"SHARD-02\"],\"state\":\"queued\",\"future_wave\":\"wave 3 after GATE-0002,GATE-0003,GATE-0004\",\"allocation_rule\":\"expand after its predecessor shards; preserve shared UI and web-adapter ownership\"},\n    {\"chapter\":\"SHARD-04\",\"title\":\"PWA delivery, performance, operations, and release evidence\",\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\",\"SHARD-02\",\"SHARD-03\"],\"state\":\"queued\",\"future_wave\":\"wave 4 after GATE-0002,GATE-0005,GATE-0007\",\"allocation_rule\":\"expand only after the session/UI and campaign contracts exist\"},\n    {\"chapter\":\"SHARD-05\",\"title\":\"Connected-scope decision package\",\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\"],\"state\":\"hold\",\"future_wave\":\"only if explicitly authorised after GATE-0006\",\"allocation_rule\":\"no P0 implementation R contracts\"}\n  ],\n  \"context_packet_baseline\": {\n    \"terminology\": [\"B-series = authoring runbook\", \"R-series = generated implementation runbook\", \"IMP-series = catalogue contract\", \"shared core\", \"web adapter\", \"PWA delivery adapter\", \"local save\", \"cache\", \"human gate\"],\n    \"target_constraints\": [\"original offline-capable 2D single-player RPG\", \"responsive web and installable PWA\", \"keyboard/mouse/touch/gamepad\", \"no accounts, sync, multiplayer, purchases, or network services in P0\", \"shared core must not import platform/render/network modules\", \"PWA cache and save data remain separate\"],\n    \"required_templates\": [\"runbooks/TEMPLATE.md\", \"runbooks/F014.md provenance and asset-assessment requirements\"],\n    \"authoring_rules\": [\"write only assigned paths\", \"preserve gates and unanswered questions\", \"do not create incidental assets when asset_impact is not_applicable\", \"perform structural, not product-release, validation\"]\n  },\n  \"batches\": [\n    {\"id\":\"B0001\",\"order\":1,\"title\":\"Bootstrap decision-gated foundation\",\"state\":\"blocked_on_gate\",\"parallel_with\":[],\"preceding_decision\":\"GATE-0001 / DEC-0001 framework, package manager, and CI selection\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0001\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/01-product-brief.md#release-definition\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/platform-appendix.md\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0001\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"validate R0001 metadata and output ownership, record gate disposition, then checkpoint wave\",\"recovery\":\"keep R0001 reserved; after the gate, rerun B0001 only\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"one bounded R runbook\",\"gate is explicit\",\"baseline command and ownership evidence are specified\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"B0002\",\"order\":2,\"title\":\"Shared seams, deterministic harness, and token contract\",\"state\":\"planned\",\"depends_on_batches\":[\"B0001\"],\"parallel_with\":[],\"preceding_decision\":\"B0001 accepted; R0012's visual-token portion remains blocked by GATE-0002,GATE-0004\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0002\",\"R0003\",\"R0010\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#layout-visual-tokens-and-responsive-behaviour\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0003\",\"IMP-0010\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"validate the three contracts and record any gate-blocked subwork\",\"recovery\":\"repair only R0002,R0003,R0010; never split or renumber accepted contracts\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"core/adapter seam precedes feature work\",\"fixture and token outputs have distinct ownership\",\"all gates retained\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"B0003\",\"order\":3,\"title\":\"Deterministic state slice and connected-scope exclusion\",\"state\":\"planned\",\"depends_on_batches\":[\"B0002\"],\"parallel_with\":[],\"preceding_decision\":\"B0002 accepted\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0004\",\"R0008\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/02-feature-model.md#domain-vocabulary-and-state-ownership\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#data-contract\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0008\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"validate state/event ownership and negative connected-scope coverage\",\"recovery\":\"retain IDs and repair the failed R contract only\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"vertical foundation slice remains independently reviewable\",\"P0 connected-service exclusion is explicit\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"B0004\",\"order\":4,\"title\":\"Content validation and local recovery protocols\",\"state\":\"planned\",\"depends_on_batches\":[\"B0003\"],\"parallel_with\":[],\"preceding_decision\":\"B0003 accepted; R0006 requires GATE-0003\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0005\",\"R0006\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/02-feature-model.md#save-recovery-and-offline-persistence\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0005\",\"IMP-0006\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"validate content/save boundaries and retained storage gate\",\"recovery\":\"retain R0005,R0006 and rerun the blocked item after its decision\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"content and save/cache ownership is separated\",\"save recovery remains a bounded foundation slice\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"B0005\",\"order\":5,\"title\":\"Migration, diagnostics, and provenance controls\",\"state\":\"planned\",\"depends_on_batches\":[\"B0004\"],\"parallel_with\":[\"B0006 after B0004 acceptance, except R0007 still waits for R0006\"],\"preceding_decision\":\"R0007 needs GATE-0003; R0009 needs GATE-0005\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0007\",\"R0009\",\"R0011\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\",\"specification/01-product-brief.md#originality-boundary\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#experience-premise-and-originality-boundary\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0007\",\"IMP-0009\",\"IMP-0011\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"validate migration, diagnostics, and provenance fields; record unresolved gates\",\"recovery\":\"rerun only incomplete assigned IDs; preserve any accepted R contract\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"no transport or remote diagnostics is introduced\",\"provenance review is explicit\",\"contracts remain at most three\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"B0006\",\"order\":6,\"title\":\"Foundation documentation closure\",\"state\":\"planned\",\"depends_on_batches\":[\"B0004\",\"B0003\"],\"parallel_with\":[\"B0005 after B0004 acceptance\"],\"preceding_decision\":\"R0006 must be accepted or documented as blocked; no gate is implicitly resolved\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0012\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0012\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"cross-check all foundation ownership, dependencies, and gates before accepting the wave\",\"recovery\":\"retain R0012 and correct only its documentation contract\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"documentation concludes the foundation slice without claiming implementation or approval\",\"gated save work remains visible\"]}\n  ],\n  \"r_contracts\": [\n    {\"id\":\"R0001\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0001\",\"title\":\"Bootstrap reproducible shared project baseline\",\"dependencies\":[],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0001.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/01-product-brief.md#release-definition\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0001\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0001\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No product asset work; establish only project/tooling boundaries and prohibit incidental assets.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"documented deterministic baseline command\",\"isolated ownership directories\",\"GATE-0001 retained\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and path; repair only this contract\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0002\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0002\",\"title\":\"Enforce shared-core and adapter dependency seams\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0001\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0002.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#dependency-direction-and-state-rules\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0002\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0002\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; this is an interface and dependency-policy contract.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"forbidden core imports rejected\",\"adapter command-only fixture\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0003\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0003\",\"title\":\"Create deterministic test and fixture harness\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0001\",\"R0002\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0003.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#observability-quality-evidence-and-release-verification\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0003\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0002\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; fixtures use non-product deterministic data.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"repeatable fixture result\",\"isolated fixture storage\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0004\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0004\",\"title\":\"Define deterministic campaign state and command contract\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0002\",\"R0003\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0004.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#data-contract\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0004\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0003\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; state envelopes deliberately exclude authored content.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"stale and invalid commands do not mutate state\",\"duplicate interaction is idempotent\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0005\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0005\",\"title\":\"Define versioned content schema and validation boundary\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0001\",\"R0003\",\"R0004\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0005.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas\",\"specification/02-feature-model.md#domain-vocabulary-and-state-ownership\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0005\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0004\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No art/audio assets; reserve only schema/provenance fields for later original assets.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"valid minimal package passes\",\"invalid references fail\",\"reachability fixture\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0006\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0006\",\"title\":\"Specify local save and recovery protocol\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0002\",\"R0003\",\"R0004\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0006.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0006\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0004\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; protocol is data/recovery only.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"fault fixtures cover write and validation failures\",\"save/cache separation\",\"GATE-0003 retained\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID; wait for storage decision before accepting gated work\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0007\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0007\",\"title\":\"Define pure save migration runner\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0005\",\"R0006\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0007\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0005\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; migration fixtures retain original bytes only.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"predecessors migrate once\",\"failed candidate remains intact\",\"GATE-0003 retained\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and resume after R0006/gate closure\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0008\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0008\",\"title\":\"Bound P0 identity, authorization, and connected-service exclusions\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0002\",\"R0004\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0008.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0008\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0003\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; a negative scope boundary.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"no identity/token/network fields\",\"future connected work remains gated\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0009\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0009\",\"title\":\"Define privacy-safe local diagnostics boundary\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0002\",\"R0003\",\"R0006\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0009.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0009\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0005\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; local redacted records only.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"consent and deletion controls\",\"payload redaction\",\"no network transport\",\"GATE-0005 retained\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and wait for privacy gate where required\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0010\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0010\",\"title\":\"Establish semantic accessibility design tokens\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0001\",\"R0002\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0010.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#layout-visual-tokens-and-responsive-behaviour\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0010\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0002\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No final artwork, fonts, or icons; semantic tokens only and prohibit incidental assets.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"non-colour cues\",\"reduced motion values\",\"GATE-0002,GATE-0004 retained\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and await numeric design decisions\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0011\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0011\",\"title\":\"Create original-content provenance control\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0005\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0011.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/01-product-brief.md#originality-boundary\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#experience-premise-and-originality-boundary\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0011\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0005\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets are created; this contract defines provenance controls for later asset-required work.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"missing provenance rejected\",\"human creative review recorded\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0012\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0012\",\"title\":\"Document foundation architecture and recovery boundaries\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0002\",\"R0004\",\"R0006\",\"R0008\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0012.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0012\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0006\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; developer-documentation closure only.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"all foundation ownership/dependencies/gates cross-checked\",\"does not claim release readiness\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this documentation contract\"}\n  ]\n}\n# 10 \u2014 Specification-to-runbook authoring handoff\n\n**Purpose:** hand the audited planning catalogue to F011\u2013F016 without starting\nproduct implementation, testing, deployment, or release activity. This file is\nan authoring control record, not an implementation plan that overrides the\n[source brief](../INITIAL.md).\n\n## Authoritative inputs and evidence locations\n\nRead these in order. If sources conflict, preserve the source brief, record the\nconflict in the F011 decision log, and stop the affected allocation rather than\ninventing a resolution.\n\n1. [INITIAL.md](../INITIAL.md) is the original source of truth; the normalized\n   [product brief](../specification/01-product-brief.md) preserves its scope.\n2. [Domain discovery](../specification/00-domain-discovery.md), the feature,\n   technical, and experience contracts (`02`\u2013`04`) define the discovered\n   product and target constraints.\n3. [Delivery map](05-delivery-map.md) provides the dependency order DM-01 to\n   DM-20. [Foundation](06-foundation-domain-contracts.md),\n   [feature](07-feature-experience-contracts.md), and\n   [quality](08-quality-operations-contracts.md) define FDN-01\u201309,\n   FEX-01\u201314, and QOR-01\u201308 ownership and acceptance evidence.\n4. [Contract audit](09-contract-audit.md) is the current closure evidence,\n   including browser-spec ownership and retained decisions.\n\nF011 writes canonical specification and traceability evidence under\n`specification/` (including `requirements.md`, `requirements.json`, a\ntraceability matrix, decision log, platform appendix, and specification index).\nF012 writes the implementation catalogue and graph under `planning/`; F013\nwrites the batch manifest there; F014 writes B-series authoring runbooks under\n`authoring-runbooks/` and their registration records; F015 writes structural\nquality-gate evidence; and F016 writes the project README and durable resume\nhandoff. Generated R-series instructions and their evidence belong in\n`runbooks/` and the locations named by their final contracts. Planned test and\nbrowser paths are ownership reservations only until a later implementation task\ncreates executable code and independent evidence.\n\n## Scope boundary and original-design rule\n\nThe P0 to author is an original, offline-capable 2D, single-player fantasy RPG:\none town, one dungeon, a guided short campaign ending, exploration, dialogue,\nquests, party-based turn-based combat, inventory/rewards, onboarding, local\nsave/load/checkpoints/recovery, settings/accessibility, responsive web, and an\ninstallable PWA with safe offline/update behaviour. It uses a shared core with\nonly necessary web/PWA adaptations.\n\nDo not author implementation work for additional regions, chapters, native\napps, PWA-exclusive rules, live events, player-created/shared content, advanced\nanalytics/monetisation, cloud sync, payment flows, accounts/identity,\nmultiplayer, moderation, player-safety services, live operations, or\nentitlements. The brief mentions several connected capabilities, but their\nconflict with the offline P0 remains an explicit hold; no author may recast\nthat hold as approved scope.\n\nThe Final Fantasy V reference permits only high-level party-based turn-based\nadventure scope. Never reproduce or request copied names, branding, assets,\nstory/lore, dialogue, maps, music, layouts, menus, combat screens, interaction\nchoreography, or distinctive presentation. All planned content and assets must\nbe independently original, warm hand-painted fantasy with readable silhouettes\nand a restrained palette, supported by provenance records and later human\nreview.\n\n## Execution order and dependencies\n\n| Stage | Required outcome | Inputs / dependency | Cannot proceed without |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| F011 | Canonical `REQ-*`, `NFR-*`, `DEC-*`, `RISK-*`, `GATE-*` system and traceability | This handoff and all specifications/planning 05\u201309 | Recording, not deciding, open choices |\n| F012 | Bounded `IMP-*` catalogue, ownership, and acyclic graph | Completed F011 | Requirement traceability and named domain shards |\n| F013 | Persistent B/R allocation ledger and context packets | Completed F012 | Unique immutable IDs and dependency-safe batches of at most seven R contracts |\n| F014 | Bootstrap B-series/dispatcher collection and child registrations | Completed F013 | Valid manifest, bounded wave, and existing-ID collision checks |\n| F015 | Structural/traceability quality gate and recovery procedure | F014 output plus manifest | Passing ownership, metadata, dependency, asset, and browser-path checks |\n| F016 | Project README, registrations, evidence map, and resume handoff | F015 quality evidence | Explicit holds and safe resume points retained |\n\nWithin later implementation contracts, preserve the DM order: select and\nbootstrap the framework before core/state/content; establish persistence and\nrecovery before session/UI; complete campaign rules before their UI; then input\nand accessibility, PWA lifecycle, release hardening, quality evidence, and\ndocumentation. Parallel authoring is allowed only for contracts whose declared\ndependencies are already satisfied and whose files/data/browser paths do not\noverlap.\n\n## Decision gates, approvals, and stop conditions\n\nThe following gates require a human or responsible external owner before a\ndependent contract is allocated as ready: engine/framework and package manager;\nCI runtime; browser storage API/quota; browser/device/assistive-tech and\nnetwork matrix; numeric performance budget; host/CDN and service-worker rollout;\ncontent quantities, party size, balance, locale, audio and remapping scope;\nfont/contrast targets; diagnostics provider/transport, retention and privacy;\nand ratings, age, regional, legal, support, store, or certification policy.\n\nStop the batch authoring system and mark the item blocked\u2014not failed or\nimplicitly approved\u2014when any of these occurs:\n\n- an open decision changes scope, privacy/security, cost, legal obligations,\n  connected services, or delivery commitments;\n- a requirement lacks a source, owner, verification approach, or safe bounded\n  contract; a dependency is cyclic or ownership conflicts;\n- an R/B/asset ID, output path, browser test path, or accepted contract would\n  be overwritten, renumbered, duplicated, or ambiguously owned;\n- a request entails credentials, paid services, account creation, store action,\n  deployment, publishing, release approval, or real-device/certification access;\n- evidence would require claiming that planned paths, generated runbooks, or\n  structural validation prove product implementation or release readiness.\n\n## Safe authoring-agent configuration\n\nUse a workspace-scoped authoring agent with no secrets, deployments, payments,\npublishing, external account actions, or authority to approve gates. Give each\nagent only its manifest context packet, the source documents it cites, its\nassigned immutable IDs, and its declared output paths. It may create Markdown,\nJSON manifests, validation instructions, and child-registration files only in\nthis project workspace; it must not create product source, generated game\nassets, tests that purport to validate a product, or release artefacts in this\nF011\u2013F016 phase.\n\nEvery authoring task records source links, requirement/contract IDs,\ndependencies, owned outputs, unresolved questions, gate status, and structural\nevidence. It checkpoints after each bounded batch, retains accepted IDs and\nmanifest counters, and resumes from the next unaccepted item. F015 is the\nstructural evidence gate: it validates metadata, traceability, dependency\nclosure, output ownership, asset assessment, and browser-path uniqueness. Any\nlater executable test, browser result, visual review, accessibility assessment,\nor release evidence must be stored at the paths named by its implementation\ncontract and remains outside this authoring handoff.\n\n## Assumptions and risks carried forward\n\nSafe assumptions are limited to an offline-first local campaign, original\ncontent/UI, shared core with necessary target adaptations, local durable saves\nwhere browser storage allows, visibly degraded connected features if ever\napproved, and privacy-minimised diagnostics. They are guardrails, not stack,\nvendor, backend, account, retention, performance, accessibility, or support\npromises.\n\nKey risks are unresolved connected-scope conflict; storage/quota and update\nloss hazards; unsupported browser/device or assistive-tech assumptions;\nunapproved performance targets; original-design/provenance failure; and\nmanifest/ID drift across resumed authoring waves. Mitigate each by retaining\nthe named gate, keeping save/cache responsibilities separated, requiring\nprovenance and human creative review, and using the F013 ledger plus F015\nquality gate before dispatching further work.\n\n## Readiness statement\n\nThe catalogue is ready for **batch authoring only**: audited inputs identify\nthe P0 boundary, contract namespaces, delivery dependencies, evidence owners,\nand unresolved decision gates. F011\u2013F016 may now formalise, shard, allocate,\nvalidate, and hand off implementation instructions. This statement does not\nselect a technology, authorize any gate, create implementation or release\nwork, or assert that the game has been built, tested, or approved for release.\n---\ntask_id: T001\nsequence: 1\ntitle: Describe one small, reviewable change\nbrowser_impact: none\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nDescribe the smallest complete outcome. State what is in scope and, equally\nimportant, what must not be changed.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- The intended behaviour is implemented and documented where it affects users or developers.\n- Focused automated tests cover the change and pass.\n- No unrelated refactors, network calls, or credentials are introduced.\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"find projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4 -maxdepth 2 -type d | sort; rg -n \\\"front matter|front_matter|task_id|parse.*runbook|load.*runbook\\\" supervisor/supervisor/runbooks.py supervisor/tests/test_runbooks.py supervisor/supervisor -g '*.py' | head -100; jq '{project_slug,expected_runbook_count,id_counters,wave,queued_expansion,batches: [.batches[]|{id,order,state,depends_on_batches,r_contract_ids}], r_contracts: [.r_contracts[]|{id,catalogue_id,dependencies,output_path,source_specifications,source_catalogue_ids,authoring_batch,factory_stages,asset_impact,asset_ids,asset_brief}]}' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/.state\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/.state/live\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/.state/reports\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification\nsupervisor/supervisor/runbooks.py:31:    required = {\"task_id\", \"sequence\", \"title\", \"browser_impact\", \"playwright_spec\"}\nsupervisor/supervisor/runbooks.py:35:    is_r_series = re.fullmatch(r\"R\\d+\", metadata[\"task_id\"]) is not None\nsupervisor/supervisor/runbooks.py:83:        task_id=metadata[\"task_id\"],\nsupervisor/tests/test_runbooks.py:10:    task = load_task(root / \"runbooks\" / \"D005.md\")\nsupervisor/tests/test_runbooks.py:11:    assert task.task_id ==