act_count\": 12,\n  \"state\": \"ready_for_authoring\",\n  \"boundary\": \"Framework-neutral seams, deterministic state/data contracts, local persistence protocol, quality foundations, and original-design controls; excludes campaign rules, UI flows, PWA lifecycle, and release execution.\"\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"IMP-0001\",\n  \"title\": \"Bootstrap reproducible shared project baseline\",\n  \"domain\": \"foundation\",\n  \"targets\": [\n    \"shared\",\n    \"web\",\n    \"pwa\"\n  ],\n  \"requirement_ids\": [\n    \"NFR-0010\",\n    \"NFR-0012\"\n  ],\n  \"bounded_outcome\": \"A framework-neutral project skeleton documents one bootstrap, lint, format, and deterministic test command with isolated shared, web-adapter, PWA-adapter, content, and test directories.\",\n  \"prerequisites\": [],\n  \"ownership\": {\n    \"files\": [\n      \"root build/tooling configuration\",\n      \"src/{core,content,app,platform/web,platform/pwa}/\",\n      \"tests/\",\n      \"docs/development.md\"\n    ],\n    \"data\": [\n      \"pinned toolchain declaration\"\n    ],\n    \"api\": [\n      \"build/test command interface\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"forbidden_scope\": [\n    \"selecting framework/package manager/CI without DEC-0001\",\n    \"gameplay\",\n    \"service worker\",\n    \"hosting\"\n  ],\n  \"verification\": \"Clean approved-runtime checkout runs the documented deterministic sample test, lint, and format checks.\",\n  \"human_external_gate\": \"GATE-0001 / DEC-0001 framework, package-manager, and CI selection before implementation.\",\n  \"complexity\": \"medium\",\n  \"status\": \"gated\"\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"IMP-0002\",\n  \"title\": \"Enforce shared-core and adapter dependency seams\",\n  \"domain\": \"foundation\",\n  \"targets\": [\n    \"shared\",\n    \"web\",\n    \"pwa\"\n  ],\n  \"requirement_ids\": [\n    \"NFR-0010\",\n    \"REQ-0013\",\n    \"NFR-0012\"\n  ],\n  \"bounded_outcome\": \"A dependency policy and public interfaces prevent core code from importing browser, renderer, clock, network, or platform modules; adapters submit commands and render returned state/events.\",\n  \"prerequisites\": [\n    \"IMP-0001\"\n  ],\n  \"ownership\": {\n    \"files\": [\n      \"src/core/public interfaces\",\n      \"src/platform/{web,pwa}/adapter interfaces\",\n      \"architecture dependency rules\",\n      \"docs/architecture.md\"\n    ],\n    \"data\": [\n\ncodex\n{\"status\":\"pass\",\"summary\":\"The manifest already allocates the first 12 foundation contracts across B0001\u2013B0006. I\u2019m materialising only those six bounded writers plus a bootstrap catalogue checkpoint and one durable dispatcher; later chapters remain dynamically allocated work.\",\"changed_files\":[],\"test_result\":\"\",\"evidence\":{\"agent_log\":\"\",\"adapter_log\":\"\",\"test_log\":\"\",\"browser_log\":\"\",\"screenshots\":[]},\"acceptance_results\":[],\"documentation\":{\"reviewed_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/10-authoring-handoff.md\",\"supervisor/supervisor/runbooks.py\"],\"updated_files\":[],\"summary\":\"Reviewed the authoring ledger, handoff, and loader requirements.\"},\"known_limitations\":[],\"browser_coverage\":\"\",\"recommended_next_step\":\"complete\"}\napply patch\npatch: completed\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0001.md\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0005.md\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0006.md\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/C0001.md\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/runbooks/.supervisor-children/mock-fantasy-quest-4.json\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..960c27ae6d9a16cbfe551f01cb096ad3a22621b3\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\n+{\"runbooks_dir\":\"../runbooks\"}\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0001.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0001.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..d44ba355dd76d32fa22b3e3bf2c7d6bb4f191032\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0001.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0001\n+sequence: 2\n+title: Author the bootstrap baseline implementation contract\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Create only `../runbooks/R0001.md` from manifest batch B0001. Its precise\n+contract is IMP-0001, \"Bootstrap reproducible shared project baseline\". It is\n+not permission to implement the game or resolve GATE-0001.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `../specification/01-product-brief.md#release-definition`,\n+`../specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability`,\n+`../planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json` (IMP-0001), and the B0001/R0001\n+manifest records. Use `../../../runbooks/TEMPLATE.md` for the Supervisor shape.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0001.md` only; metadata must use `task_id: R0001`, `sequence: 1`, `source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0001`, `authoring_batch: B0001`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`, and the manifest provenance/asset values.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Give R0001 a small, precise objective; dependencies; relevant requirement IDs;\n+owned files, data, and interfaces; required behaviour; non-goals; web/PWA\n+platform differences; verification commands and evidence; observable acceptance\n+criteria; and an `## Asset assessment` explaining that no asset is needed and\n+incidental asset creation is prohibited. Include all required standard front\n+matter, including `asset_impact: not_applicable`, blank `asset_ids`, and the\n+non-empty provenance fields exactly as the manifest records them.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Before writing, stop if R0001 exists with a different ID, catalogue mapping,\n+provenance, dependency set, or output owner. After writing, load it with\n+`supervisor.runbooks.load_task`, compare every metadata value and dependency\n+against the manifest, and confirm it has all required sections.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update only B0001's manifest state/checkpoint after successful validation.\n+Retain R0001 and its ID on any failure; repair that one path on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after R0001. Do not create another R file, choose a framework, or pass GATE-0001.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Exactly one R-series runbook, R0001, is created for the allocated IMP-0001 contract.\n+- R0001 is a bounded implementation task with the required sections, metadata, provenance, and explicit no-asset assessment.\n+- Existing conflicting R0001 content causes a stop and report rather than an overwrite.\n+- Manifest ownership and checkpoint state are updated only after structural validation passes.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..0a3720f34d5f48722a12d3de51c3ce95686cd624\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0002\n+sequence: 3\n+title: Author shared seams and deterministic harness contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Create only `../runbooks/R0002.md`, `../runbooks/R0003.md`, and\n+`../runbooks/R0010.md` for B0002. They map respectively to IMP-0002, IMP-0003,\n+and IMP-0010; B0001 must be accepted first.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, the B0002 manifest record, its three catalogue\n+records, and only these specification sections: `03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency`,\n+`04-experience-contract.md#layout-visual-tokens-and-responsive-behaviour`, and\n+`04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0002.md` \u2014 IMP-0002; dependencies R0001.\n+- `../runbooks/R0003.md` \u2014 IMP-0003; dependencies R0001,R0002.\n+- `../runbooks/R0010.md` \u2014 IMP-0010; dependencies R0001,R0002.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+For each output, use standard Supervisor front matter and the exact manifest\n+provenance (`source_specifications`, `source_catalogue_ids`, `authoring_batch:\n+B0002`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`) plus `asset_impact:\n+not_applicable` and blank `asset_ids`. Make each an individually implementable\n+task containing objective, dependencies, relevant requirements, ownership,\n+behaviour, non-goals, web/PWA differences, verification/evidence, observable\n+acceptance criteria, and an `## Asset assessment` that prohibits incidental\n+assets.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Refuse a conflicting existing R ID or path. Load every output, compare all\n+metadata and dependencies to the manifest, verify provenance fields are\n+non-empty, and verify that all three outputs have the required sections.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update only B0002's checkpoint/state after all three outputs validate. Preserve\n+accepted outputs and repair only the failed assigned file on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after these three files; do not resolve the retained design gates or write another R-series contract.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- R0002, R0003, and R0010 are the only outputs and each maps to its assigned IMP record.\n+- Each output is bounded, traceable, dependency-correct, and explicitly prohibits incidental asset work.\n+- Metadata, required sections, and manifest ownership are structurally validated before checkpointing.\n+- ID or ownership mismatches stop the batch without overwrite or renumbering.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..90fb845c6600aaad53d4748c781f372585b282e0\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0003\n+sequence: 4\n+title: Author deterministic state and connected-scope exclusion contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0002, create only `../runbooks/R0004.md` and `../runbooks/R0008.md`\n+for IMP-0004 and IMP-0008.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, the B0003/R0004/R0008 manifest records, the two\n+catalogue records, and `02-feature-model.md#domain-vocabulary-and-state-ownership`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#data-contract`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency`, and\n+`03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0004.md` \u2014 IMP-0004; dependencies R0002,R0003.\n+- `../runbooks/R0008.md` \u2014 IMP-0008; dependencies R0002,R0004.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use exact manifest provenance with `authoring_batch: B0003`, standard\n+Supervisor metadata, and `asset_impact: not_applicable` with blank\n+`asset_ids`. Each R file must include precise objective, dependencies,\n+requirements, files/data/interfaces, required behaviour, non-goals, platform\n+differences, verification/evidence, observable acceptance criteria, and an\n+`## Asset assessment` that explains no visual/source asset is needed and\n+prohibits incidental creation.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Stop on an existing conflicting R ID/path. Load both files; compare metadata,\n+provenance, dependencies, and ownership with the manifest; and verify every\n+required section before updating state.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Checkpoint B0003 only when both R files validate. Retain IDs and repair only\n+the failed output on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after R0004 and R0008; do not create services, identity, accounts, or more R files.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Exactly R0004 and R0008 are authored for their allocated IMP records.\n+- Both outputs are small, dependency-correct, fully traceable contracts with explicit no-asset assessments.\n+- Conflicting existing work stops authoring without overwrite or ID reuse.\n+- The manifest is checkpointed only after both outputs load and match it.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..2c5f4b2fd378f1ee4282e7baf11e456fbf3737d6\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0004\n+sequence: 5\n+title: Author content-validation and local recovery contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0003, create only `../runbooks/R0005.md` and `../runbooks/R0006.md`\n+for IMP-0005 and IMP-0006; retain GATE-0003.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read the B0004/R0005/R0006 manifest records, the two catalogue records,\n+`../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics`,\n+`02-feature-model.md#save-recovery-and-offline-persistence`, and\n+`04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0005.md` \u2014 IMP-0005; dependencies R0001,R0003,R0004.\n+- `../runbooks/R0006.md` \u2014 IMP-0006; dependencies R0002,R0003,R0004.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use standard front matter, exact manifest provenance (`authoring_batch: B0004`),\n+and `asset_impact: not_applicable` with blank `asset_ids`. Each output must\n+cover objective, dependencies, requirements, ownership, behaviour, non-goals,\n+platform differences, verification/evidence, observable acceptance criteria,\n+and an `## Asset assessment` forbidding incidental asset creation.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Never overwrite a conflicting R file. Load and compare both files with the\n+manifest, including provenance and dependencies, then verify required sections\n+and GATE-0003 retention.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update B0004 only after both structural checks pass; preserve IDs and repair\n+only the failed output if resumed.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after two outputs. Do not select browser storage or claim the save gate is approved.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- R0005 and R0006 are the only generated contracts and match their two IMP allocations.\n+- Both contracts retain the save/storage gate and make no incidental asset work.\n+- Loader, provenance, dependency, ownership, and required-section validation completes before checkpointing.\n+- A mismatch stops rather than overwrites an R contract.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0005.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0005.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..8db7a73ae46c480e7e5e4ec70874bd45b737b4c8\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0005.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0005\n+sequence: 6\n+title: Author migration diagnostics and provenance contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0004, create only `../runbooks/R0007.md`, `../runbooks/R0009.md`, and\n+`../runbooks/R0011.md` for IMP-0007, IMP-0009, and IMP-0011. Retain all named\n+human gates.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read the B0005/R0007/R0009/R0011 manifest records and catalogue records,\n+`../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security`,\n+`01-product-brief.md#originality-boundary`, and\n+`04-experience-contract.md#experience-premise-and-originality-boundary`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0007.md` \u2014 IMP-0007; dependencies R0005,R0006.\n+- `../runbooks/R0009.md` \u2014 IMP-0009; dependencies R0002,R0003,R0006.\n+- `../runbooks/R0011.md` \u2014 IMP-0011; dependency R0005.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use standard front matter and exact manifest provenance with `authoring_batch:\n+B0005`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`, `asset_impact: not_applicable`, and\n+blank `asset_ids`. Each small R task must provide objective, dependencies,\n+requirements, files/data/interfaces, required behaviour, non-goals, platform\n+differences, verification/evidence, observable criteria, and an `## Asset\n+assessment` prohibiting incidental asset creation.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Stop on an existing conflicting R ID/path. Load all three and compare their\n+metadata, dependencies, provenance, and ownership to the manifest; verify\n+required sections and retained GATE-0003/GATE-0005 status.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Checkpoint B0005 only after every assigned output validates. Keep accepted\n+outputs and repair only an incomplete assigned path on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after the three listed files. Do not introduce remote diagnostics, assets, or services.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Exactly R0007, R0009, and R0011 are generated for their allocated IMP records.\n+- Each R contract is bounded, traceable, dependency-correct, and has an explicit no-asset assessment.\n+- Conflicts halt without overwriting, renumbering, or assigning a replacement ID.\n+- The manifest checkpoint follows successful loader and manifest comparison only.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0006.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0006.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..cdf87c05bb005aad12679a309634f9b10c0e589b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0006.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0006\n+sequence: 7\n+title: Author the foundation documentation closure contract\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0003 and B0004, create only `../runbooks/R0012.md` for IMP-0012. It\n+documents foundation architecture/recovery boundaries without claiming product\n+implementation, approval, or release readiness.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, the B0006/R0012 manifest and catalogue records,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics`, and\n+`03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0012.md` \u2014 IMP-0012; dependencies R0002,R0004,R0006,R0008.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use standard front matter with the exact manifest provenance (`authoring_batch:\n+B0006`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`), `asset_impact: not_applicable`, and\n+blank `asset_ids`. Include objective, dependencies, requirements, ownership,\n+required behaviour, non-goals, platform differences, verification/evidence,\n+observable criteria, and an `## Asset assessment` explaining why no asset is\n+needed and prohibiting incidental assets.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Stop rather than overwrite a conflicting R0012. Load it, compare all metadata,\n+provenance, dependencies, and ownership to the manifest, and check every\n+required section and explicit retained gate.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update B0006 only after validation. Retain the reserved ID and repair only this\n+file on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after R0012; do not write a final audit or allocate another R contract.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- R0012 is the only output and maps exactly to IMP-0012.\n+- It is a bounded, loader-valid, fully traceable contract with a no-asset assessment.\n+- A conflicting existing contract is reported without overwrite or ID reuse.\n+- Checkpointing follows successful manifest comparison only.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/C0001.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/C0001.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..95e2200e33659c79dda4e2542bfa570ec224cd8c\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/C0001.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@\n+---\n+task_id: C0001\n+sequence: 1\n+title: Validate the bounded foundation catalogue bootstrap\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Validate the existing `SHARD-01` implementation catalogue before authoring.\n+Read only the canonical specification, `planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json`,\n+and `planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`. Confirm that SHARD-01 contains\n+at most 250 `IMP-*` contracts, that every ready foundation contract is allocated\n+once, and that SHARD-02 through SHARD-05 remain queued or held. Do not expand a\n+future chapter, create R-series files, or change accepted IDs.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Check unique `IMP-*`, B, and R IDs; contract-to-manifest coverage; dependency\n+closure; the 250-contract bound; and that B0001 through B0006 each contain no\n+more than seven R IDs. Record only factual repairs to the manifest/ledger when\n+the sources agree. Stop and report any missing canonical source, conflicting\n+ownership, cyclic dependency, or attempt to allocate a held connected-scope\n+chapter.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Set the manifest wave checkpoint only after the structural checks pass. Preserve\n+all counters and existing allocations; append a short checkpoint note to the\n+ledger if it does not already describe the result. Leave future allocation to\n+D0001.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- SHARD-01 is verified as a bounded catalogue of no more than 250 contracts.\n+- The twelve foundation `IMP-*` records are each allocated exactly once to B0001 through B0006, with no batch over seven R contracts.\n+- Queued and held chapters remain unexpanded and no R-series implementation runbook is created.\n+- Conflicts, missing sources, cycles, or ID collisions stop the task without renumbering or overwriting work.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..735a844029d6d1831759e0691eeaf4519fea26e1\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,73 @@\n+---\n+task_id: D0001\n+sequence: 8\n+title: Dispatch the next bounded implementation-runbook authoring wave\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Run one durable authoring-dispatch iteration after the bootstrap B0001\u2013B0006\n+wave. First expand at most one eligible queued specification/catalogue chapter\n+into no more than 250 `IMP-*` records and validate its requirement/dependency\n+coverage. Then allocate ready, unassigned contracts into at most ten new\n+B-series authoring tasks, each with at most seven R-series outputs. Create\n+exactly one successor dispatcher when a queued chapter or ready contract\n+remains; create the final audit B-series task instead only when neither exists.\n+Exit after creating that bounded set.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `INITIAL.md`, `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `../specification/README.md`,\n+`../planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json`,\n+`../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`, its Markdown ledger, and\n+`../../../runbooks/F014.md`. Read only the canonical specification sections\n+needed for the one selected chapter. Treat SHARD-05 as held unless explicit\n+authorisation is recorded; do not turn a gate into approval.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Select no more than one queued chapter whose dependencies and gates permit\n+planning. Add at most 250 stable `IMP-*` contracts with requirement links,\n+owned files/data/interfaces, dependencies, non-goals, platform distinctions,\n+verification, asset assessment, and canonical source links. Validate coverage,\n+unique IDs, ownership, and acyclic dependencies. Allocate only ready\n+unassigned contracts, using monotonic B/R counters and batches of no more than\n+seven R IDs; materialise at most ten corresponding B runbooks. Each B writer\n+must contain a context packet, output list, validation procedure,\n+checkpoint/update procedure, collision stop rule, and stop condition. Do not\n+create R-series files yourself.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Atomically update the JSON/Markdown ledger counters, chapter state, contract\n+allocations, and checkpoint after validation. Never renumber, replace, or\n+rewrite an accepted B/R contract. If work remains, create exactly one new\n+dispatcher with the next monotonic dispatcher ID and a later sequence. If no\n+queued chapter or ready contract remains, create exactly one final audit\n+B-series runbook that validates all completed catalogue expansions and batches;\n+it must not pretend to generate or review all work in this dispatch.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Validate JSON, the 250-contract chapter cap, no more than ten newly-created B\n+files, no more than seven assigned R IDs per B file, unique B/R/IMP IDs,\n+dependency closure, provenance values, asset metadata, output ownership, and\n+the successor/final-audit choice. Stop and report a source conflict, missing\n+coverage, cycle, ID/path collision, unresolved authority, or any need to\n+overwrite accepted work.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop immediately after one chapter expansion (or none), one allocation wave,\n+and exactly one successor dispatcher or final audit task. This is not a\n+recursive prompt and must not materialise a whole-game plan.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- This iteration expands at most one eligible chapter and adds no more than 250 IMP contracts.\n+- It creates at most ten bounded B-series authoring tasks, each with at most seven assigned R-series outputs.\n+- Every created B task has its context packet, output list, validation, checkpoint/update, collision protection, and stop condition.\n+- If queued or ready work remains, exactly one successor dispatcher is created; otherwise exactly one final audit B-series task is created.\n+- IDs, manifest ownership, provenance, asset assessments, and dependencies are validated without overwriting accepted work.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..5e24170a9f17243df4715c1ab64fdb1d57f52d9b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@\n+# Implementation-runbook authoring context\n+\n+This collection creates implementation instructions only. The canonical project\n+scope is [PROJECT_BRIEF.md](../PROJECT_BRIEF.md); read the canonical\n+[specification](../specification/README.md) and the allocation ledger at\n+[`../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`](../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json)\n+before writing an R-series file. Do not infer, approve, or implement unresolved\n+decisions. This collection is a child of the factory collection and its R-series\n+output is registered as its own child collection.\n+\n+The initial wave is deliberately limited to the already allocated SHARD-01\n+foundation contracts. Future work is created only by the dispatcher, one\n+catalogue chapter and at most ten B-series tasks at a time.\ndiff --git a/runbooks/.supervisor-children/mock-fantasy-quest-4.json b/runbooks/.supervisor-children/mock-fantasy-quest-4.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..06eefe3c3f6bfb75799bd665798dfd3c8424bb21\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/runbooks/.supervisor-children/mock-fantasy-quest-4.json\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\n+{\"runbooks_dir\":\"../projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks\"}\n\nhook: PostToolUse\nhook: PostToolUse Failed\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..960c27ae6d9a16cbfe551f01cb096ad3a22621b3\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\n+{\"runbooks_dir\":\"../runbooks\"}\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0001.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0001.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..d44ba355dd76d32fa22b3e3bf2c7d6bb4f191032\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0001.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0001\n+sequence: 2\n+title: Author the bootstrap baseline implementation contract\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Create only `../runbooks/R0001.md` from manifest batch B0001. Its precise\n+contract is IMP-0001, \"Bootstrap reproducible shared project baseline\". It is\n+not permission to implement the game or resolve GATE-0001.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `../specification/01-product-brief.md#release-definition`,\n+`../specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability`,\n+`../planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json` (IMP-0001), and the B0001/R0001\n+manifest records. Use `../../../runbooks/TEMPLATE.md` for the Supervisor shape.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0001.md` only; metadata must use `task_id: R0001`, `sequence: 1`, `source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0001`, `authoring_batch: B0001`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`, and the manifest provenance/asset values.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Give R0001 a small, precise objective; dependencies; relevant requirement IDs;\n+owned files, data, and interfaces; required behaviour; non-goals; web/PWA\n+platform differences; verification commands and evidence; observable acceptance\n+criteria; and an `## Asset assessment` explaining that no asset is needed and\n+incidental asset creation is prohibited. Include all required standard front\n+matter, including `asset_impact: not_applicable`, blank `asset_ids`, and the\n+non-empty provenance fields exactly as the manifest records them.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Before writing, stop if R0001 exists with a different ID, catalogue mapping,\n+provenance, dependency set, or output owner. After writing, load it with\n+`supervisor.runbooks.load_task`, compare every metadata value and dependency\n+against the manifest, and confirm it has all required sections.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update only B0001's manifest state/checkpoint after successful validation.\n+Retain R0001 and its ID on any failure; repair that one path on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after R0001. Do not create another R file, choose a framework, or pass GATE-0001.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Exactly one R-series runbook, R0001, is created for the allocated IMP-0001 contract.\n+- R0001 is a bounded implementation task with the required sections, metadata, provenance, and explicit no-asset assessment.\n+- Existing conflicting R0001 content causes a stop and report rather than an overwrite.\n+- Manifest ownership and checkpoint state are updated only after structural validation passes.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..0a3720f34d5f48722a12d3de51c3ce95686cd624\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0002\n+sequence: 3\n+title: Author shared seams and deterministic harness contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Create only `../runbooks/R0002.md`, `../runbooks/R0003.md`, and\n+`../runbooks/R0010.md` for B0002. They map respectively to IMP-0002, IMP-0003,\n+and IMP-0010; B0001 must be accepted first.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, the B0002 manifest record, its three catalogue\n+records, and only these specification sections: `03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency`,\n+`04-experience-contract.md#layout-visual-tokens-and-responsive-behaviour`, and\n+`04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0002.md` \u2014 IMP-0002; dependencies R0001.\n+- `../runbooks/R0003.md` \u2014 IMP-0003; dependencies R0001,R0002.\n+- `../runbooks/R0010.md` \u2014 IMP-0010; dependencies R0001,R0002.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+For each output, use standard Supervisor front matter and the exact manifest\n+provenance (`source_specifications`, `source_catalogue_ids`, `authoring_batch:\n+B0002`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`) plus `asset_impact:\n+not_applicable` and blank `asset_ids`. Make each an individually implementable\n+task containing objective, dependencies, relevant requirements, ownership,\n+behaviour, non-goals, web/PWA differences, verification/evidence, observable\n+acceptance criteria, and an `## Asset assessment` that prohibits incidental\n+assets.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Refuse a conflicting existing R ID or path. Load every output, compare all\n+metadata and dependencies to the manifest, verify provenance fields are\n+non-empty, and verify that all three outputs have the required sections.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update only B0002's checkpoint/state after all three outputs validate. Preserve\n+accepted outputs and repair only the failed assigned file on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after these three files; do not resolve the retained design gates or write another R-series contract.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- R0002, R0003, and R0010 are the only outputs and each maps to its assigned IMP record.\n+- Each output is bounded, traceable, dependency-correct, and explicitly prohibits incidental asset work.\n+- Metadata, required sections, and manifest ownership are structurally validated before checkpointing.\n+- ID or ownership mismatches stop the batch without overwrite or renumbering.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..90fb845c6600aaad53d4748c781f372585b282e0\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0003\n+sequence: 4\n+title: Author deterministic state and connected-scope exclusion contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0002, create only `../runbooks/R0004.md` and `../runbooks/R0008.md`\n+for IMP-0004 and IMP-0008.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, the B0003/R0004/R0008 manifest records, the two\n+catalogue records, and `02-feature-model.md#domain-vocabulary-and-state-ownership`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#data-contract`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency`, and\n+`03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0004.md` \u2014 IMP-0004; dependencies R0002,R0003.\n+- `../runbooks/R0008.md` \u2014 IMP-0008; dependencies R0002,R0004.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use exact manifest provenance with `authoring_batch: B0003`, standard\n+Supervisor metadata, and `asset_impact: not_applicable` with blank\n+`asset_ids`. Each R file must include precise objective, dependencies,\n+requirements, files/data/interfaces, required behaviour, non-goals, platform\n+differences, verification/evidence, observable acceptance criteria, and an\n+`## Asset assessment` that explains no visual/source asset is needed and\n+prohibits incidental creation.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Stop on an existing conflicting R ID/path. Load both files; compare metadata,\n+provenance, dependencies, and ownership with the manifest; and verify every\n+required section before updating state.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Checkpoint B0003 only when both R files validate. Retain IDs and repair only\n+the failed output on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after R0004 and R0008; do not create services, identity, accounts, or more R files.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Exactly R0004 and R0008 are authored for their allocated IMP records.\n+- Both outputs are small, dependency-correct, fully traceable contracts with explicit no-asset assessments.\n+- Conflicting existing work stops authoring without overwrite or ID reuse.\n+- The manifest is checkpointed only after both outputs load and match it.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..2c5f4b2fd378f1ee4282e7baf11e456fbf3737d6\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0004\n+sequence: 5\n+title: Author content-validation and local recovery contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0003, create only `../runbooks/R0005.md` and `../runbooks/R0006.md`\n+for IMP-0005 and IMP-0006; retain GATE-0003.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read the B0004/R0005/R0006 manifest records, the two catalogue records,\n+`../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics`,\n+`02-feature-model.md#save-recovery-and-offline-persistence`, and\n+`04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0005.md` \u2014 IMP-0005; dependencies R0001,R0003,R0004.\n+- `../runbooks/R0006.md` \u2014 IMP-0006; dependencies R0002,R0003,R0004.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use standard front matter, exact manifest provenance (`authoring_batch: B0004`),\n+and `asset_impact: not_applicable` with blank `asset_ids`. Each output must\n+cover objective, dependencies, requirements, ownership, behaviour, non-goals,\n+platform differences, verification/evidence, observable acceptance criteria,\n+and an `## Asset assessment` forbidding incidental asset creation.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Never overwrite a conflicting R file. Load and compare both files with the\n+manifest, including provenance and dependencies, then verify required sections\n+and GATE-0003 retention.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update B0004 only after both structural checks pass; preserve IDs and repair\n+only the failed output if resumed.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after two outputs. Do not select browser storage or claim the save gate is approved.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- R0005 and R0006 are the only generated contracts and match their two IMP allocations.\n+- Both contracts retain the save/storage gate and make no incidental asset work.\n+- Loader, provenance, dependency, ownership, and required-section validation completes before checkpointing.\n+- A mismatch stops rather than overwrites an R contract.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0005.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0005.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..8db7a73ae46c480e7e5e4ec70874bd45b737b4c8\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0005.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0005\n+sequence: 6\n+title: Author migration diagnostics and provenance contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0004, create only `../runbooks/R0007.md`, `../runbooks/R0009.md`, and\n+`../runbooks/R0011.md` for IMP-0007, IMP-0009, and IMP-0011. Retain all named\n+human gates.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read the B0005/R0007/R0009/R0011 manifest records and catalogue records,\n+`../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security`,\n+`01-product-brief.md#originality-boundary`, and\n+`04-experience-contract.md#experience-premise-and-originality-boundary`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0007.md` \u2014 IMP-0007; dependencies R0005,R0006.\n+- `../runbooks/R0009.md` \u2014 IMP-0009; dependencies R0002,R0003,R0006.\n+- `../runbooks/R0011.md` \u2014 IMP-0011; dependency R0005.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use standard front matter and exact manifest provenance with `authoring_batch:\n+B0005`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`, `asset_impact: not_applicable`, and\n+blank `asset_ids`. Each small R task must provide objective, dependencies,\n+requirements, files/data/interfaces, required behaviour, non-goals, platform\n+differences, verification/evidence, observable criteria, and an `## Asset\n+assessment` prohibiting incidental asset creation.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Stop on an existing conflicting R ID/path. Load all three and compare their\n+metadata, dependencies, provenance, and ownership to the manifest; verify\n+required sections and retained GATE-0003/GATE-0005 status.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Checkpoint B0005 only after every assigned output validates. Keep accepted\n+outputs and repair only an incomplete assigned path on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after the three listed files. Do not introduce remote diagnostics, assets, or services.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Exactly R0007, R0009, and R0011 are generated for their allocated IMP records.\n+- Each R contract is bounded, traceable, dependency-correct, and has an explicit no-asset assessment.\n+- Conflicts halt without overwriting, renumbering, or assigning a replacement ID.\n+- The manifest checkpoint follows successful loader and manifest comparison only.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0006.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0006.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..cdf87c05bb005aad12679a309634f9b10c0e589b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0006.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0006\n+sequence: 7\n+title: Author the foundation documentation closure contract\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0003 and B0004, create only `../runbooks/R0012.md` for IMP-0012. It\n+documents foundation architecture/recovery boundaries without claiming product\n+implementation, approval, or release readiness.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, the B0006/R0012 manifest and catalogue records,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics`, and\n+`03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0012.md` \u2014 IMP-0012; dependencies R0002,R0004,R0006,R0008.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use standard front matter with the exact manifest provenance (`authoring_batch:\n+B0006`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`), `asset_impact: not_applicable`, and\n+blank `asset_ids`. Include objective, dependencies, requirements, ownership,\n+required behaviour, non-goals, platform differences, verification/evidence,\n+observable criteria, and an `## Asset assessment` explaining why no asset is\n+needed and prohibiting incidental assets.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Stop rather than overwrite a conflicting R0012. Load it, compare all metadata,\n+provenance, dependencies, and ownership to the manifest, and check every\n+required section and explicit retained gate.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update B0006 only after validation. Retain the reserved ID and repair only this\n+file on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after R0012; do not write a final audit or allocate another R contract.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- R0012 is the only output and maps exactly to IMP-0012.\n+- It is a bounded, loader-valid, fully traceable contract with a no-asset assessment.\n+- A conflicting existing contract is reported without overwrite or ID reuse.\n+- Checkpointing follows successful manifest comparison only.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/C0001.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/C0001.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..95e2200e33659c79dda4e2542bfa570ec224cd8c\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/C0001.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@\n+---\n+task_id: C0001\n+sequence: 1\n+title: Validate the bounded foundation catalogue bootstrap\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Validate the existing `SHARD-01` implementation catalogue before authoring.\n+Read only the canonical specification, `planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json`,\n+and `planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`. Confirm that SHARD-01 contains\n+at most 250 `IMP-*` contracts, that every ready foundation contract is allocated\n+once, and that SHARD-02 through SHARD-05 remain queued or held. Do not expand a\n+future chapter, create R-series files, or change accepted IDs.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Check unique `IMP-*`, B, and R IDs; contract-to-manifest coverage; dependency\n+closure; the 250-contract bound; and that B0001 through B0006 each contain no\n+more than seven R IDs. Record only factual repairs to the manifest/ledger when\n+the sources agree. Stop and report any missing canonical source, conflicting\n+ownership, cyclic dependency, or attempt to allocate a held connected-scope\n+chapter.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Set the manifest wave checkpoint only after the structural checks pass. Preserve\n+all counters and existing allocations; append a short checkpoint note to the\n+ledger if it does not already describe the result. Leave future allocation to\n+D0001.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- SHARD-01 is verified as a bounded catalogue of no more than 250 contracts.\n+- The twelve foundation `IMP-*` records are each allocated exactly once to B0001 through B0006, with no batch over seven R contracts.\n+- Queued and held chapters remain unexpanded and no R-series implementation runbook is created.\n+- Conflicts, missing sources, cycles, or ID collisions stop the task without renumbering or overwriting work.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..735a844029d6d1831759e0691eeaf4519fea26e1\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,73 @@\n+---\n+task_id: D0001\n+sequence: 8\n+title: Dispatch the next bounded implementation-runbook authoring wave\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Run one durable authoring-dispatch iteration after the bootstrap B0001\u2013B0006\n+wave. First expand at most one eligible queued specification/catalogue chapter\n+into no more than 250 `IMP-*` records and validate its requirement/dependency\n+coverage. Then allocate ready, unassigned contracts into at most ten new\n+B-series authoring tasks, each with at most seven R-series outputs. Create\n+exactly one successor dispatcher when a queued chapter or ready contract\n+remains; create the final audit B-series task instead only when neither exists.\n+Exit after creating that bounded set.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `INITIAL.md`, `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `../specification/README.md`,\n+`../planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json`,\n+`../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`, its Markdown ledger, and\n+`../../../runbooks/F014.md`. Read only the canonical specification sections\n+needed for the one selected chapter. Treat SHARD-05 as held unless explicit\n+authorisation is recorded; do not turn a gate into approval.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Select no more than one queued chapter whose dependencies and gates permit\n+planning. Add at most 250 stable `IMP-*` contracts with requirement links,\n+owned files/data/interfaces, dependencies, non-goals, platform distinctions,\n+verification, asset assessment, and canonical source links. Validate coverage,\n+unique IDs, ownership, and acyclic dependencies. Allocate only ready\n+unassigned contracts, using monotonic B/R counters and batches of no more than\n+seven R IDs; materialise at most ten corresponding B runbooks. Each B writer\n+must contain a context packet, output list, validation procedure,\n+checkpoint/update procedure, collision stop rule, and stop condition. Do not\n+create R-series files yourself.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Atomically update the JSON/Markdown ledger counters, chapter state, contract\n+allocations, and checkpoint after validation. Never renumber, replace, or\n+rewrite an accepted B/R contract. If work remains, create exactly one new\n+dispatcher with the next monotonic dispatcher ID and a later sequence. If no\n+queued chapter or ready contract remains, create exactly one final audit\n+B-series runbook that validates all completed catalogue expansions and batches;\n+it must not pretend to generate or review all work in this dispatch.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Validate JSON, the 250-contract chapter cap, no more than ten newly-created B\n+files, no more than seven assigned R IDs per B file, unique B/R/IMP IDs,\n+dependency closure, provenance values, asset metadata, output ownership, and\n+the successor/final-audit choice. Stop and report a source conflict, missing\n+coverage, cycle, ID/path collision, unresolved authority, or any need to\n+overwrite accepted work.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop immediately after one chapter expansion (or none), one allocation wave,\n+and exactly one successor dispatcher or final audit task. This is not a\n+recursive prompt and must not materialise a whole-game plan.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- This iteration expands at most one eligible chapter and adds no more than 250 IMP contracts.\n+- It creates at most ten bounded B-series authoring tasks, each with at most seven assigned R-series outputs.\n+- Every created B task has its context packet, output list, validation, checkpoint/update, collision protection, and stop condition.\n+- If queued or ready work remains, exactly one successor dispatcher is created; otherwise exactly one final audit B-series task is created.\n+- IDs, manifest ownership, provenance, asset assessments, and dependencies are validated without overwriting accepted work.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..5e24170a9f17243df4715c1ab64fdb1d57f52d9b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@\n+# Implementation-runbook authoring context\n+\n+This collection creates implementation instructions only. The canonical project\n+scope is [PROJECT_BRIEF.md](../PROJECT_BRIEF.md); read the canonical\n+[specification](../specification/README.md) and the allocation ledger at\n+[`../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`](../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json)\n+before writing an R-series file. Do not infer, approve, or implement unresolved\n+decisions. This collection is a child of the factory collection and its R-series\n+output is registered as its own child collection.\n+\n+The initial wave is deliberately limited to the already allocated SHARD-01\n+foundation contracts. Future work is created only by the dispatcher, one\n+catalogue chapter and at most ten B-series tasks at a time.\ndiff --git a/runbooks/.supervisor-children/mock-fantasy-quest-4.json b/runbooks/.supervisor-children/mock-fantasy-quest-4.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..06eefe3c3f6bfb75799bd665798dfd3c8424bb21\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/runbooks/.supervisor-children/mock-fantasy-quest-4.json\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\n+{\"runbooks_dir\":\"../projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks\"}\n\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..960c27ae6d9a16cbfe551f01cb096ad3a22621b3\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\n+{\"runbooks_dir\":\"../runbooks\"}\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0001.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0001.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..d44ba355dd76d32fa22b3e3bf2c7d6bb4f191032\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0001.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0001\n+sequence: 2\n+title: Author the bootstrap baseline implementation contract\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Create only `../runbooks/R0001.md` from manifest batch B0001. Its precise\n+contract is IMP-0001, \"Bootstrap reproducible shared project baseline\". It is\n+not permission to implement the game or resolve GATE-0001.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `../specification/01-product-brief.md#release-definition`,\n+`../specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability`,\n+`../planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json` (IMP-0001), and the B0001/R0001\n+manifest records. Use `../../../runbooks/TEMPLATE.md` for the Supervisor shape.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0001.md` only; metadata must use `task_id: R0001`, `sequence: 1`, `source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0001`, `authoring_batch: B0001`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`, and the manifest provenance/asset values.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Give R0001 a small, precise objective; dependencies; relevant requirement IDs;\n+owned files, data, and interfaces; required behaviour; non-goals; web/PWA\n+platform differences; verification commands and evidence; observable acceptance\n+criteria; and an `## Asset assessment` explaining that no asset is needed and\n+incidental asset creation is prohibited. Include all required standard front\n+matter, including `asset_impact: not_applicable`, blank `asset_ids`, and the\n+non-empty provenance fields exactly as the manifest records them.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Before writing, stop if R0001 exists with a different ID, catalogue mapping,\n+provenance, dependency set, or output owner. After writing, load it with\n+`supervisor.runbooks.load_task`, compare every metadata value and dependency\n+against the manifest, and confirm it has all required sections.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update only B0001's manifest state/checkpoint after successful validation.\n+Retain R0001 and its ID on any failure; repair that one path on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after R0001. Do not create another R file, choose a framework, or pass GATE-0001.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Exactly one R-series runbook, R0001, is created for the allocated IMP-0001 contract.\n+- R0001 is a bounded implementation task with the required sections, metadata, provenance, and explicit no-asset assessment.\n+- Existing conflicting R0001 content causes a stop and report rather than an overwrite.\n+- Manifest ownership and checkpoint state are updated only after structural validation passes.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..0a3720f34d5f48722a12d3de51c3ce95686cd624\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0002\n+sequence: 3\n+title: Author shared seams and deterministic harness contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Create only `../runbooks/R0002.md`, `../runbooks/R0003.md`, and\n+`../runbooks/R0010.md` for B0002. They map respectively to IMP-0002, IMP-0003,\n+and IMP-0010; B0001 must be accepted first.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, the B0002 manifest record, its three catalogue\n+records, and only these specification sections: `03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency`,\n+`04-experience-contract.md#layout-visual-tokens-and-responsive-behaviour`, and\n+`04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0002.md` \u2014 IMP-0002; dependencies R0001.\n+- `../runbooks/R0003.md` \u2014 IMP-0003; dependencies R0001,R0002.\n+- `../runbooks/R0010.md` \u2014 IMP-0010; dependencies R0001,R0002.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+For each output, use standard Supervisor front matter and the exact manifest\n+provenance (`source_specifications`, `source_catalogue_ids`, `authoring_batch:\n+B0002`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`) plus `asset_impact:\n+not_applicable` and blank `asset_ids`. Make each an individually implementable\n+task containing objective, dependencies, relevant requirements, ownership,\n+behaviour, non-goals, web/PWA differences, verification/evidence, observable\n+acceptance criteria, and an `## Asset assessment` that prohibits incidental\n+assets.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Refuse a conflicting existing R ID or path. Load every output, compare all\n+metadata and dependencies to the manifest, verify provenance fields are\n+non-empty, and verify that all three outputs have the required sections.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update only B0002's checkpoint/state after all three outputs validate. Preserve\n+accepted outputs and repair only the failed assigned file on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after these three files; do not resolve the retained design gates or write another R-series contract.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- R0002, R0003, and R0010 are the only outputs and each maps to its assigned IMP record.\n+- Each output is bounded, traceable, dependency-correct, and explicitly prohibits incidental asset work.\n+- Metadata, required sections, and manifest ownership are structurally validated before checkpointing.\n+- ID or ownership mismatches stop the batch without overwrite or renumbering.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..90fb845c6600aaad53d4748c781f372585b282e0\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0003\n+sequence: 4\n+title: Author deterministic state and connected-scope exclusion contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0002, create only `../runbooks/R0004.md` and `../runbooks/R0008.md`\n+for IMP-0004 and IMP-0008.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, the B0003/R0004/R0008 manifest records, the two\n+catalogue records, and `02-feature-model.md#domain-vocabulary-and-state-ownership`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#data-contract`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency`, and\n+`03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0004.md` \u2014 IMP-0004; dependencies R0002,R0003.\n+- `../runbooks/R0008.md` \u2014 IMP-0008; dependencies R0002,R0004.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use exact manifest provenance with `authoring_batch: B0003`, standard\n+Supervisor metadata, and `asset_impact: not_applicable` with blank\n+`asset_ids`. Each R file must include precise objective, dependencies,\n+requirements, files/data/interfaces, required behaviour, non-goals, platform\n+differences, verification/evidence, observable acceptance criteria, and an\n+`## Asset assessment` that explains no visual/source asset is needed and\n+prohibits incidental creation.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Stop on an existing conflicting R ID/path. Load both files; compare metadata,\n+provenance, dependencies, and ownership with the manifest; and verify every\n+required section before updating state.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Checkpoint B0003 only when both R files validate. Retain IDs and repair only\n+the failed output on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after R0004 and R0008; do not create services, identity, accounts, or more R files.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Exactly R0004 and R0008 are authored for their allocated IMP records.\n+- Both outputs are small, dependency-correct, fully traceable contracts with explicit no-asset assessments.\n+- Conflicting existing work stops authoring without overwrite or ID reuse.\n+- The manifest is checkpointed only after both outputs load and match it.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..2c5f4b2fd378f1ee4282e7baf11e456fbf3737d6\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0004\n+sequence: 5\n+title: Author content-validation and local recovery contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0003, create only `../runbooks/R0005.md` and `../runbooks/R0006.md`\n+for IMP-0005 and IMP-0006; retain GATE-0003.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read the B0004/R0005/R0006 manifest records, the two catalogue records,\n+`../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics`,\n+`02-feature-model.md#save-recovery-and-offline-persistence`, and\n+`04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0005.md` \u2014 IMP-0005; dependencies R0001,R0003,R0004.\n+- `../runbooks/R0006.md` \u2014 IMP-0006; dependencies R0002,R0003,R0004.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use standard front matter, exact manifest provenance (`authoring_batch: B0004`),\n+and `asset_impact: not_applicable` with blank `asset_ids`. Each output must\n+cover objective, dependencies, requirements, ownership, behaviour, non-goals,\n+platform differences, verification/evidence, observable acceptance criteria,\n+and an `## Asset assessment` forbidding incidental asset creation.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Never overwrite a conflicting R file. Load and compare both files with the\n+manifest, including provenance and dependencies, then verify required sections\n+and GATE-0003 retention.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update B0004 only after both structural checks pass; preserve IDs and repair\n+only the failed output if resumed.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after two outputs. Do not select browser storage or claim the save gate is approved.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- R0005 and R0006 are the only generated contracts and match their two IMP allocations.\n+- Both contracts retain the save/storage gate and make no incidental asset work.\n+- Loader, provenance, dependency, ownership, and required-section validation completes before checkpointing.\n+- A mismatch stops rather than overwrites an R contract.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0005.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0005.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..8db7a73ae46c480e7e5e4ec70874bd45b737b4c8\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0005.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0005\n+sequence: 6\n+title: Author migration diagnostics and provenance contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0004, create only `../runbooks/R0007.md`, `../runbooks/R0009.md`, and\n+`../runbooks/R0011.md` for IMP-0007, IMP-0009, and IMP-0011. Retain all named\n+human gates.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read the B0005/R0007/R0009/R0011 manifest records and catalogue records,\n+`../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security`,\n+`01-product-brief.md#originality-boundary`, and\n+`04-experience-contract.md#experience-premise-and-originality-boundary`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0007.md` \u2014 IMP-0007; dependencies R0005,R0006.\n+- `../runbooks/R0009.md` \u2014 IMP-0009; dependencies R0002,R0003,R0006.\n+- `../runbooks/R0011.md` \u2014 IMP-0011; dependency R0005.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use standard front matter and exact manifest provenance with `authoring_batch:\n+B0005`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`, `asset_impact: not_applicable`, and\n+blank `asset_ids`. Each small R task must provide objective, dependencies,\n+requirements, files/data/interfaces, required behaviour, non-goals, platform\n+differences, verification/evidence, observable criteria, and an `## Asset\n+assessment` prohibiting incidental asset creation.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Stop on an existing conflicting R ID/path. Load all three and compare their\n+metadata, dependencies, provenance, and ownership to the manifest; verify\n+required sections and retained GATE-0003/GATE-0005 status.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Checkpoint B0005 only after every assigned output validates. Keep accepted\n+outputs and repair only an incomplete assigned path on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after the three listed files. Do not introduce remote diagnostics, assets, or services.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Exactly R0007, R0009, and R0011 are generated for their allocated IMP records.\n+- Each R contract is bounded, traceable, dependency-correct, and has an explicit no-asset assessment.\n+- Conflicts halt without overwriting, renumbering, or assigning a replacement ID.\n+- The manifest checkpoint follows successful loader and manifest comparison only.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0006.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0006.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..cdf87c05bb005aad12679a309634f9b10c0e589b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0006.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0006\n+sequence: 7\n+title: Author the foundation documentation closure contract\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0003 and B0004, create only `../runbooks/R0012.md` for IMP-0012. It\n+documents foundation architecture/recovery boundaries without claiming product\n+implementation, approval, or release readiness.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, the B0006/R0012 manifest and catalogue records,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics`, and\n+`03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0012.md` \u2014 IMP-0012; dependencies R0002,R0004,R0006,R0008.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use standard front matter with the exact manifest provenance (`authoring_batch:\n+B0006`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`), `asset_impact: not_applicable`, and\n+blank `asset_ids`. Include objective, dependencies, requirements, ownership,\n+required behaviour, non-goals, platform differences, verification/evidence,\n+observable criteria, and an `## Asset assessment` explaining why no asset is\n+needed and prohibiting incidental assets.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Stop rather than overwrite a conflicting R0012. Load it, compare all metadata,\n+provenance, dependencies, and ownership to the manifest, and check every\n+required section and explicit retained gate.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update B0006 only after validation. Retain the reserved ID and repair only this\n+file on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after R0012; do not write a final audit or allocate another R contract.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- R0012 is the only output and maps exactly to IMP-0012.\n+- It is a bounded, loader-valid, fully traceable contract with a no-asset assessment.\n+- A conflicting existing contract is reported without overwrite or ID reuse.\n+- Checkpointing follows successful manifest comparison only.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/C0001.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/C0001.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..95e2200e33659c79dda4e2542bfa570ec224cd8c\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/C0001.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@\n+---\n+task_id: C0001\n+sequence: 1\n+title: Validate the bounded foundation catalogue bootstrap\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Validate the existing `SHARD-01` implementation catalogue before authoring.\n+Read only the canonical specification, `planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json`,\n+and `planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`. Confirm that SHARD-01 contains\n+at most 250 `IMP-*` contracts, that every ready foundation contract is allocated\n+once, and that SHARD-02 through SHARD-05 remain queued or held. Do not expand a\n+future chapter, create R-series files, or change accepted IDs.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Check unique `IMP-*`, B, and R IDs; contract-to-manifest coverage; dependency\n+closure; the 250-contract bound; and that B0001 through B0006 each contain no\n+more than seven R IDs. Record only factual repairs to the manifest/ledger when\n+the sources agree. Stop and report any missing canonical source, conflicting\n+ownership, cyclic dependency, or attempt to allocate a held connected-scope\n+chapter.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Set the manifest wave checkpoint only after the structural checks pass. Preserve\n+all counters and existing allocations; append a short checkpoint note to the\n+ledger if it does not already describe the result. Leave future allocation to\n+D0001.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- SHARD-01 is verified as a bounded catalogue of no more than 250 contracts.\n+- The twelve foundation `IMP-*` records are each allocated exactly once to B0001 through B0006, with no batch over seven R contracts.\n+- Queued and held chapters remain unexpanded and no R-series implementation runbook is created.\n+- Conflicts, missing sources, cycles, or ID collisions stop the task without renumbering or overwriting work.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..735a844029d6d1831759e0691eeaf4519fea26e1\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,73 @@\n+---\n+task_id: D0001\n+sequence: 8\n+title: Dispatch the next bounded implementation-runbook authoring wave\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Run one durable authoring-dispatch iteration after the bootstrap B0001\u2013B0006\n+wave. First expand at most one eligible queued specification/catalogue chapter\n+into no more than 250 `IMP-*` records and validate its requirement/dependency\n+coverage. Then allocate ready, unassigned contracts into at most ten new\n+B-series authoring tasks, each with at most seven R-series outputs. Create\n+exactly one successor dispatcher when a queued chapter or ready contract\n+remains; create the final audit B-series task instead only when neither exists.\n+Exit after creating that bounded set.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `INITIAL.md`, `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `../specification/README.md`,\n+`../planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json`,\n+`../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`, its Markdown ledger, and\n+`../../../runbooks/F014.md`. Read only the canonical specification sections\n+needed for the one selected chapter. Treat SHARD-05 as held unless explicit\n+authorisation is recorded; do not turn a gate into approval.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Select no more than one queued chapter whose dependencies and gates permit\n+planning. Add at most 250 stable `IMP-*` contracts with requirement links,\n+owned files/data/interfaces, dependencies, non-goals, platform distinctions,\n+verification, asset assessment, and canonical source links. Validate coverage,\n+unique IDs, ownership, and acyclic dependencies. Allocate only ready\n+unassigned contracts, using monotonic B/R counters and batches of no more than\n+seven R IDs; materialise at most ten corresponding B runbooks. Each B writer\n+must contain a context packet, output list, validation procedure,\n+checkpoint/update procedure, collision stop rule, and stop condition. Do not\n+create R-series files yourself.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Atomically update the JSON/Markdown ledger counters, chapter state, contract\n+allocations, and checkpoint after validation. Never renumber, replace, or\n+rewrite an accepted B/R contract. If work remains, create exactly one new\n+dispatcher with the next monotonic dispatcher ID and a later sequence. If no\n+queued chapter or ready contract remains, create exactly one final audit\n+B-series runbook that validates all completed catalogue expansions and batches;\n+it must not pretend to generate or review all work in this dispatch.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Validate JSON, the 250-contract chapter cap, no more than ten newly-created B\n+files, no more than seven assigned R IDs per B file, unique B/R/IMP IDs,\n+dependency closure, provenance values, asset metadata, output ownership, and\n+the successor/final-audit choice. Stop and report a source conflict, missing\n+coverage, cycle, ID/path collision, unresolved authority, or any need to\n+overwrite accepted work.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop immediately after one chapter expansion (or none), one allocation wave,\n+and exactly one successor dispatcher or final audit task. This is not a\n+recursive prompt and must not materialise a whole-game plan.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- This iteration expands at most one eligible chapter and adds no more than 250 IMP contracts.\n+- It creates at most ten bounded B-series authoring tasks, each with at most seven assigned R-series outputs.\n+- Every created B task has its context packet, output list, validation, checkpoint/update, collision protection, and stop condition.\n+- If queued or ready work remains, exactly one successor dispatcher is created; otherwise exactly one final audit B-series task is created.\n+- IDs, manifest ownership, provenance, asset assessments, and dependencies are validated without overwriting accepted work.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..5e24170a9f17243df4715c1ab64fdb1d57f52d9b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@\n+# Implementation-runbook authoring context\n+\n+This collection creates implementation instructions only. The canonical project\n+scope is [PROJECT_BRIEF.md](../PROJECT_BRIEF.md); read the canonical\n+[specification](../specification/README.md) and the allocation ledger at\n+[`../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`](../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json)\n+before writing an R-series file. Do not infer, approve, or implement unresolved\n+decisions. This collection is a child of the factory collection and its R-series\n+output is registered as its own child collection.\n+\n+The initial wave is deliberately limited to the already allocated SHARD-01\n+foundation contracts. Future work is created only by the dispatcher, one\n+catalogue chapter and at most ten B-series tasks at a time.\ndiff --git a/runbooks/.supervisor-children/mock-fantasy-quest-4.json b/runbooks/.supervisor-children/mock-fantasy-quest-4.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..06eefe3c3f6bfb75799bd665798dfd3c8424bb21\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/runbooks/.supervisor-children/mock-fantasy-quest-4.json\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\n+{\"runbooks_dir\":\"../projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks\"}\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"PYTHONPATH=supervisor python -c 'from pathlib import Path; from supervisor.runbooks import load_task; files=sorted(Path(\\\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks\\\").glob(\\\"[BCD][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9].md\\\")); [load_task(p) for p in files]; print(\\\"loaded\\\", \\\", \\\".join(p.stem for p in files))' && python -c 'import json; from pathlib import Path; root=Path(\\\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4\\\"); a=json.loads((Path(\\\"runbooks/.supervisor-children/mock-fantasy-quest-4.json\\\")).read_text()); b=json.loads((root/\\\"authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json\\\").read_text()); assert a=={\\\"runbooks_dir\\\":\\\"../projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks\\\"}; assert b=={\\\"runbooks_dir\\\":\\\"../runbooks\\\"}; assert (Path(\\\"runbooks\\\")/a[\\\"runbooks_dir\\\"]).resolve()==(root/\\\"authoring-runbooks\\\").resolve(); assert ((root/\\\"authoring-runbooks\\\")/b[\\\"runbooks_dir\\\"]).resolve()==(root/\\\"runbooks\\\").resolve(); print(\\\"child registrations valid\\\")' && node -e 'const fs=require(\\\"fs\\\"),m=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(\\\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\\\")); const ids=new Set(m.r_contracts.map(x=>x.id)); if(ids.size\"'!==m.r_contracts.length||m.batches.some(x=>x.r_contract_ids.length>7)||m.r_contracts.some(x=>!x.source_specifications.length||!x.source_catalogue_ids.length||!x.authoring_batch||!x.factory_stages.length||!x.asset_impact||!Array.isArray(x.asset_ids))) process.exit(1); console.log(\"manifest bounds and provenance valid\")'\"' && git diff --check && git status --short\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n exited 127 in 0ms:\nzsh:1: command not found: python\n\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..960c27ae6d9a16cbfe551f01cb096ad3a22621b3\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\n+{\"runbooks_dir\":\"../runbooks\"}\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0001.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0001.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..d44ba355dd76d32fa22b3e3bf2c7d6bb4f191032\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0001.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0001\n+sequence: 2\n+title: Author the bootstrap baseline implementation contract\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Create only `../runbooks/R0001.md` from manifest batch B0001. Its precise\n+contract is IMP-0001, \"Bootstrap reproducible shared project baseline\". It is\n+not permission to implement the game or resolve GATE-0001.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `../specification/01-product-brief.md#release-definition`,\n+`../specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability`,\n+`../planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json` (IMP-0001), and the B0001/R0001\n+manifest records. Use `../../../runbooks/TEMPLATE.md` for the Supervisor shape.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0001.md` only; metadata must use `task_id: R0001`, `sequence: 1`, `source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0001`, `authoring_batch: B0001`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`, and the manifest provenance/asset values.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Give R0001 a small, precise objective; dependencies; relevant requirement IDs;\n+owned files, data, and interfaces; required behaviour; non-goals; web/PWA\n+platform differences; verification commands and evidence; observable acceptance\n+criteria; and an `## Asset assessment` explaining that no asset is needed and\n+incidental asset creation is prohibited. Include all required standard front\n+matter, including `asset_impact: not_applicable`, blank `asset_ids`, and the\n+non-empty provenance fields exactly as the manifest records them.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Before writing, stop if R0001 exists with a different ID, catalogue mapping,\n+provenance, dependency set, or output owner. After writing, load it with\n+`supervisor.runbooks.load_task`, compare every metadata value and dependency\n+against the manifest, and confirm it has all required sections.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update only B0001's manifest state/checkpoint after successful validation.\n+Retain R0001 and its ID on any failure; repair that one path on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after R0001. Do not create another R file, choose a framework, or pass GATE-0001.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Exactly one R-series runbook, R0001, is created for the allocated IMP-0001 contract.\n+- R0001 is a bounded implementation task with the required sections, metadata, provenance, and explicit no-asset assessment.\n+- Existing conflicting R0001 content causes a stop and report rather than an overwrite.\n+- Manifest ownership and checkpoint state are updated only after structural validation passes.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..0a3720f34d5f48722a12d3de51c3ce95686cd624\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0002\n+sequence: 3\n+title: Author shared seams and deterministic harness contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Create only `../runbooks/R0002.md`, `../runbooks/R0003.md`, and\n+`../runbooks/R0010.md` for B0002. They map respectively to IMP-0002, IMP-0003,\n+and IMP-0010; B0001 must be accepted first.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, the B0002 manifest record, its three catalogue\n+records, and only these specification sections: `03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency`,\n+`04-experience-contract.md#layout-visual-tokens-and-responsive-behaviour`, and\n+`04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0002.md` \u2014 IMP-0002; dependencies R0001.\n+- `../runbooks/R0003.md` \u2014 IMP-0003; dependencies R0001,R0002.\n+- `../runbooks/R0010.md` \u2014 IMP-0010; dependencies R0001,R0002.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+For each output, use standard Supervisor front matter and the exact manifest\n+provenance (`source_specifications`, `source_catalogue_ids`, `authoring_batch:\n+B0002`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`) plus `asset_impact:\n+not_applicable` and blank `asset_ids`. Make each an individually implementable\n+task containing objective, dependencies, relevant requirements, ownership,\n+behaviour, non-goals, web/PWA differences, verification/evidence, observable\n+acceptance criteria, and an `## Asset assessment` that prohibits incidental\n+assets.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Refuse a conflicting existing R ID or path. Load every output, compare all\n+metadata and dependencies to the manifest, verify provenance fields are\n+non-empty, and verify that all three outputs have the required sections.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update only B0002's checkpoint/state after all three outputs validate. Preserve\n+accepted outputs and repair only the failed assigned file on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after these three files; do not resolve the retained design gates or write another R-series contract.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- R0002, R0003, and R0010 are the only outputs and each maps to its assigned IMP record.\n+- Each output is bounded, traceable, dependency-correct, and explicitly prohibits incidental asset work.\n+- Metadata, required sections, and manifest ownership are structurally validated before checkpointing.\n+- ID or ownership mismatches stop the batch without overwrite or renumbering.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..90fb845c6600aaad53d4748c781f372585b282e0\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0003\n+sequence: 4\n+title: Author deterministic state and connected-scope exclusion contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0002, create only `../runbooks/R0004.md` and `../runbooks/R0008.md`\n+for IMP-0004 and IMP-0008.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, the B0003/R0004/R0008 manifest records, the two\n+catalogue records, and `02-feature-model.md#domain-vocabulary-and-state-ownership`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#data-contract`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency`, and\n+`03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0004.md` \u2014 IMP-0004; dependencies R0002,R0003.\n+- `../runbooks/R0008.md` \u2014 IMP-0008; dependencies R0002,R0004.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use exact manifest provenance with `authoring_batch: B0003`, standard\n+Supervisor metadata, and `asset_impact: not_applicable` with blank\n+`asset_ids`. Each R file must include precise objective, dependencies,\n+requirements, files/data/interfaces, required behaviour, non-goals, platform\n+differences, verification/evidence, observable acceptance criteria, and an\n+`## Asset assessment` that explains no visual/source asset is needed and\n+prohibits incidental creation.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Stop on an existing conflicting R ID/path. Load both files; compare metadata,\n+provenance, dependencies, and ownership with the manifest; and verify every\n+required section before updating state.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Checkpoint B0003 only when both R files validate. Retain IDs and repair only\n+the failed output on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after R0004 and R0008; do not create services, identity, accounts, or more R files.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Exactly R0004 and R0008 are authored for their allocated IMP records.\n+- Both outputs are small, dependency-correct, fully traceable contracts with explicit no-asset assessments.\n+- Conflicting existing work stops authoring without overwrite or ID reuse.\n+- The manifest is checkpointed only after both outputs load and match it.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..2c5f4b2fd378f1ee4282e7baf11e456fbf3737d6\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0004\n+sequence: 5\n+title: Author content-validation and local recovery contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0003, create only `../runbooks/R0005.md` and `../runbooks/R0006.md`\n+for IMP-0005 and IMP-0006; retain GATE-0003.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read the B0004/R0005/R0006 manifest records, the two catalogue records,\n+`../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics`,\n+`02-feature-model.md#save-recovery-and-offline-persistence`, and\n+`04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0005.md` \u2014 IMP-0005; dependencies R0001,R0003,R0004.\n+- `../runbooks/R0006.md` \u2014 IMP-0006; dependencies R0002,R0003,R0004.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use standard front matter, exact manifest provenance (`authoring_batch: B0004`),\n+and `asset_impact: not_applicable` with blank `asset_ids`. Each output must\n+cover objective, dependencies, requirements, ownership, behaviour, non-goals,\n+platform differences, verification/evidence, observable acceptance criteria,\n+and an `## Asset assessment` forbidding incidental asset creation.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Never overwrite a conflicting R file. Load and compare both files with the\n+manifest, including provenance and dependencies, then verify required sections\n+and GATE-0003 retention.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update B0004 only after both structural checks pass; preserve IDs and repair\n+only the failed output if resumed.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after two outputs. Do not select browser storage or claim the save gate is approved.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- R0005 and R0006 are the only generated contracts and match their two IMP allocations.\n+- Both contracts retain the save/storage gate and make no incidental asset work.\n+- Loader, provenance, dependency, ownership, and required-section validation completes before checkpointing.\n+- A mismatch stops rather than overwrites an R contract.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0005.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0005.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..8db7a73ae46c480e7e5e4ec70874bd45b737b4c8\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0005.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0005\n+sequence: 6\n+title: Author migration diagnostics and provenance contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0004, create only `../runbooks/R0007.md`, `../runbooks/R0009.md`, and\n+`../runbooks/R0011.md` for IMP-0007, IMP-0009, and IMP-0011. Retain all named\n+human gates.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read the B0005/R0007/R0009/R0011 manifest records and catalogue records,\n+`../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security`,\n+`01-product-brief.md#originality-boundary`, and\n+`04-experience-contract.md#experience-premise-and-originality-boundary`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0007.md` \u2014 IMP-0007; dependencies R0005,R0006.\n+- `../runbooks/R0009.md` \u2014 IMP-0009; dependencies R0002,R0003,R0006.\n+- `../runbooks/R0011.md` \u2014 IMP-0011; dependency R0005.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use standard front matter and exact manifest provenance with `authoring_batch:\n+B0005`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`, `asset_impact: not_applicable`, and\n+blank `asset_ids`. Each small R task must provide objective, dependencies,\n+requirements, files/data/interfaces, required behaviour, non-goals, platform\n+differences, verification/evidence, observable criteria, and an `## Asset\n+assessment` prohibiting incidental asset creation.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Stop on an existing conflicting R ID/path. Load all three and compare their\n+metadata, dependencies, provenance, and ownership to the manifest; verify\n+required sections and retained GATE-0003/GATE-0005 status.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Checkpoint B0005 only after every assigned output validates. Keep accepted\n+outputs and repair only an incomplete assigned path on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after the three listed files. Do not introduce remote diagnostics, assets, or services.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Exactly R0007, R0009, and R0011 are generated for their allocated IMP records.\n+- Each R contract is bounded, traceable, dependency-correct, and has an explicit no-asset assessment.\n+- Conflicts halt without overwriting, renumbering, or assigning a replacement ID.\n+- The manifest checkpoint follows successful loader and manifest comparison only.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0006.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0006.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..cdf87c05bb005aad12679a309634f9b10c0e589b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0006.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0006\n+sequence: 7\n+title: Author the foundation documentation closure contract\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0003 and B0004, create only `../runbooks/R0012.md` for IMP-0012. It\n+documents foundation architecture/recovery boundaries without claiming product\n+implementation, approval, or release readiness.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, the B0006/R0012 manifest and catalogue records,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics`, and\n+`03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0012.md` \u2014 IMP-0012; dependencies R0002,R0004,R0006,R0008.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use standard front matter with the exact manifest provenance (`authoring_batch:\n+B0006`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`), `asset_impact: not_applicable`, and\n+blank `asset_ids`. Include objective, dependencies, requirements, ownership,\n+required behaviour, non-goals, platform differences, verification/evidence,\n+observable criteria, and an `## Asset assessment` explaining why no asset is\n+needed and prohibiting incidental assets.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Stop rather than overwrite a conflicting R0012. Load it, compare all metadata,\n+provenance, dependencies, and ownership to the manifest, and check every\n+required section and explicit retained gate.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update B0006 only after validation. Retain the reserved ID and repair only this\n+file on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after R0012; do not write a final audit or allocate another R contract.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- R0012 is the only output and maps exactly to IMP-0012.\n+- It is a bounded, loader-valid, fully traceable contract with a no-asset assessment.\n+- A conflicting existing contract is reported without overwrite or ID reuse.\n+- Checkpointing follows successful manifest comparison only.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/C0001.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/C0001.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..95e2200e33659c79dda4e2542bfa570ec224cd8c\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/C0001.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@\n+---\n+task_id: C0001\n+sequence: 1\n+title: Validate the bounded foundation catalogue bootstrap\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Validate the existing `SHARD-01` implementation catalogue before authoring.\n+Read only the canonical specification, `planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json`,\n+and `planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`. Confirm that SHARD-01 contains\n+at most 250 `IMP-*` contracts, that every ready foundation contract is allocated\n+once, and that SHARD-02 through SHARD-05 remain queued or held. Do not expand a\n+future chapter, create R-series files, or change accepted IDs.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Check unique `IMP-*`, B, and R IDs; contract-to-manifest coverage; dependency\n+closure; the 250-contract bound; and that B0001 through B0006 each contain no\n+more than seven R IDs. Record only factual repairs to the manifest/ledger when\n+the sources agree. Stop and report any missing canonical source, conflicting\n+ownership, cyclic dependency, or attempt to allocate a held connected-scope\n+chapter.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Set the manifest wave checkpoint only after the structural checks pass. Preserve\n+all counters and existing allocations; append a short checkpoint note to the\n+ledger if it does not already describe the result. Leave future allocation to\n+D0001.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- SHARD-01 is verified as a bounded catalogue of no more than 250 contracts.\n+- The twelve foundation `IMP-*` records are each allocated exactly once to B0001 through B0006, with no batch over seven R contracts.\n+- Queued and held chapters remain unexpanded and no R-series implementation runbook is created.\n+- Conflicts, missing sources, cycles, or ID collisions stop the task without renumbering or overwriting work.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..735a844029d6d1831759e0691eeaf4519fea26e1\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,73 @@\n+---\n+task_id: D0001\n+sequence: 8\n+title: Dispatch the next bounded implementation-runbook authoring wave\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Run one durable authoring-dispatch iteration after the bootstrap B0001\u2013B0006\n+wave. First expand at most one eligible queued specification/catalogue chapter\n+into no more than 250 `IMP-*` records and validate its requirement/dependency\n+coverage. Then allocate ready, unassigned contracts into at most ten new\n+B-series authoring tasks, each with at most seven R-series outputs. Create\n+exactly one successor dispatcher when a queued chapter or ready contract\n+remains; create the final audit B-series task instead only when neither exists.\n+Exit after creating that bounded set.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `INITIAL.md`, `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `../specification/README.md`,\n+`../planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json`,\n+`../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`, its Markdown ledger, and\n+`../../../runbooks/F014.md`. Read only the canonical specification sections\n+needed for the one selected chapter. Treat SHARD-05 as held unless explicit\n+authorisation is recorded; do not turn a gate into approval.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Select no more than one queued chapter whose dependencies and gates permit\n+planning. Add at most 250 stable `IMP-*` contracts with requirement links,\n+owned files/data/interfaces, dependencies, non-goals, platform distinctions,\n+verification, asset assessment, and canonical source links. Validate coverage,\n+unique IDs, ownership, and acyclic dependencies. Allocate only ready\n+unassigned contracts, using monotonic B/R counters and batches of no more than\n+seven R IDs; materialise at most ten corresponding B runbooks. Each B writer\n+must contain a context packet, output list, validation procedure,\n+checkpoint/update procedure, collision stop rule, and stop condition. Do not\n+create R-series files yourself.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Atomically update the JSON/Markdown ledger counters, chapter state, contract\n+allocations, and checkpoint after validation. Never renumber, replace, or\n+rewrite an accepted B/R contract. If work remains, create exactly one new\n+dispatcher with the next monotonic dispatcher ID and a later sequence. If no\n+queued chapter or ready contract remains, create exactly one final audit\n+B-series runbook that validates all completed catalogue expansions and batches;\n+it must not pretend to generate or review all work in this dispatch.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Validate JSON, the 250-contract chapter cap, no more than ten newly-created B\n+files, no more than seven assigned R IDs per B file, unique B/R/IMP IDs,\n+dependency closure, provenance values, asset metadata, output ownership, and\n+the successor/final-audit choice. Stop and report a source conflict, missing\n+coverage, cycle, ID/path collision, unresolved authority, or any need to\n+overwrite accepted work.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop immediately after one chapter expansion (or none), one allocation wave,\n+and exactly one successor dispatcher or final audit task. This is not a\n+recursive prompt and must not materialise a whole-game plan.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- This iteration expands at most one eligible chapter and adds no more than 250 IMP contracts.\n+- It creates at most ten bounded B-series authoring tasks, each with at most seven assigned R-series outputs.\n+- Every created B task has its context packet, output list, validation, checkpoint/update, collision protection, and stop condition.\n+- If queued or ready work remains, exactly one successor dispatcher is created; otherwise exactly one final audit B-series task is created.\n+- IDs, manifest ownership, provenance, asset assessments, and dependencies are validated without overwriting accepted work.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..5e24170a9f17243df4715c1ab64fdb1d57f52d9b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@\n+# Implementation-runbook authoring context\n+\n+This collection creates implementation instructions only. The canonical project\n+scope is [PROJECT_BRIEF.md](../PROJECT_BRIEF.md); read the canonical\n+[specification](../specification/README.md) and the allocation ledger at\n+[`../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`](../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json)\n+before writing an R-series file. Do not infer, approve, or implement unresolved\n+decisions. This collection is a child of the factory collection and its R-series\n+output is registered as its own child collection.\n+\n+The initial wave is deliberately limited to the already allocated SHARD-01\n+foundation contracts. Future work is created only by the dispatcher, one\n+catalogue chapter and at most ten B-series tasks at a time.\ndiff --git a/runbooks/.supervisor-children/mock-fantasy-quest-4.json b/runbooks/.supervisor-children/mock-fantasy-quest-4.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..06eefe3c3f6bfb75799bd665798dfd3c8424bb21\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/runbooks/.supervisor-children/mock-fantasy-quest-4.json\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\n+{\"runbooks_dir\":\"../projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks\"}\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"PYTHONPATH=supervisor python3 -c 'from pathlib import Path; from supervisor.runbooks import load_task; files=sorted(Path(\\\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks\\\").glob(\\\"[BCD][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9].md\\\")); [load_task(p) for p in files]; print(\\\"loaded\\\", \\\", \\\".join(p.stem for p in files))' && python3 -c 'import json; from pathlib import Path; root=Path(\\\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4\\\"); a=json.loads((Path(\\\"runbooks/.supervisor-children/mock-fantasy-quest-4.json\\\")).read_text()); b=json.loads((root/\\\"authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json\\\").read_text()); assert a=={\\\"runbooks_dir\\\":\\\"../projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks\\\"}; assert b=={\\\"runbooks_dir\\\":\\\"../runbooks\\\"}; assert (Path(\\\"runbooks\\\")/a[\\\"runbooks_dir\\\"]).resolve()==(root/\\\"authoring-runbooks\\\").resolve(); assert ((root/\\\"authoring-runbooks\\\")/b[\\\"runbooks_dir\\\"]).resolve()==(root/\\\"runbooks\\\").resolve(); print(\\\"child registrations valid\\\")' && node -e 'const fs=require(\\\"fs\\\"),m=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(\\\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\\\")); const ids=new Set(m.r_contracts.map(x=>x.id)); if(ids.size\"'!==m.r_contracts.length||m.batches.some(x=>x.r_contract_ids.length>7)||m.r_contracts.some(x=>!x.source_specifications.length||!x.source_catalogue_ids.length||!x.authoring_batch||!x.factory_stages.length||!x.asset_impact||!Array.isArray(x.asset_ids))) process.exit(1); console.log(\"manifest bounds and provenance valid\")'\"' && git diff --check && git status --short\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..960c27ae6d9a16cbfe551f01cb096ad3a22621b3\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\n+{\"runbooks_dir\":\"../runbooks\"}\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0001.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0001.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..d44ba355dd76d32fa22b3e3bf2c7d6bb4f191032\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0001.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0001\n+sequence: 2\n+title: Author the bootstrap baseline implementation contract\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Create only `../runbooks/R0001.md` from manifest batch B0001. Its precise\n+contract is IMP-0001, \"Bootstrap reproducible shared project baseline\". It is\n+not permission to implement the game or resolve GATE-0001.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `../specification/01-product-brief.md#release-definition`,\n+`../specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability`,\n+`../planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json` (IMP-0001), and the B0001/R0001\n+manifest records. Use `../../../runbooks/TEMPLATE.md` for the Supervisor shape.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0001.md` only; metadata must use `task_id: R0001`, `sequence: 1`, `source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0001`, `authoring_batch: B0001`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`, and the manifest provenance/asset values.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Give R0001 a small, precise objective; dependencies; relevant requirement IDs;\n+owned files, data, and interfaces; required behaviour; non-goals; web/PWA\n+platform differences; verification commands and evidence; observable acceptance\n+criteria; and an `## Asset assessment` explaining that no asset is needed and\n+incidental asset creation is prohibited. Include all required standard front\n+matter, including `asset_impact: not_applicable`, blank `asset_ids`, and the\n+non-empty provenance fields exactly as the manifest records them.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Before writing, stop if R0001 exists with a different ID, catalogue mapping,\n+provenance, dependency set, or output owner. After writing, load it with\n+`supervisor.runbooks.load_task`, compare every metadata value and dependency\n+against the manifest, and confirm it has all required sections.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update only B0001's manifest state/checkpoint after successful validation.\n+Retain R0001 and its ID on any failure; repair that one path on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after R0001. Do not create another R file, choose a framework, or pass GATE-0001.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Exactly one R-series runbook, R0001, is created for the allocated IMP-0001 contract.\n+- R0001 is a bounded implementation task with the required sections, metadata, provenance, and explicit no-asset assessment.\n+- Existing conflicting R0001 content causes a stop and report rather than an overwrite.\n+- Manifest ownership and checkpoint state are updated only after structural validation passes.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..0a3720f34d5f48722a12d3de51c3ce95686cd624\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0002\n+sequence: 3\n+title: Author shared seams and deterministic harness contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Create only `../runbooks/R0002.md`, `../runbooks/R0003.md`, and\n+`../runbooks/R0010.md` for B0002. They map respectively to IMP-0002, IMP-0003,\n+and IMP-0010; B0001 must be accepted first.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, the B0002 manifest record, its three catalogue\n+records, and only these specification sections: `03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency`,\n+`04-experience-contract.md#layout-visual-tokens-and-responsive-behaviour`, and\n+`04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0002.md` \u2014 IMP-0002; dependencies R0001.\n+- `../runbooks/R0003.md` \u2014 IMP-0003; dependencies R0001,R0002.\n+- `../runbooks/R0010.md` \u2014 IMP-0010; dependencies R0001,R0002.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+For each output, use standard Supervisor front matter and the exact manifest\n+provenance (`source_specifications`, `source_catalogue_ids`, `authoring_batch:\n+B0002`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`) plus `asset_impact:\n+not_applicable` and blank `asset_ids`. Make each an individually implementable\n+task containing objective, dependencies, relevant requirements, ownership,\n+behaviour, non-goals, web/PWA differences, verification/evidence, observable\n+acceptance criteria, and an `## Asset assessment` that prohibits incidental\n+assets.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Refuse a conflicting existing R ID or path. Load every output, compare all\n+metadata and dependencies to the manifest, verify provenance fields are\n+non-empty, and verify that all three outputs have the required sections.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update only B0002's checkpoint/state after all three outputs validate. Preserve\n+accepted outputs and repair only the failed assigned file on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after these three files; do not resolve the retained design gates or write another R-series contract.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- R0002, R0003, and R0010 are the only outputs and each maps to its assigned IMP record.\n+- Each output is bounded, traceable, dependency-correct, and explicitly prohibits incidental asset work.\n+- Metadata, required sections, and manifest ownership are structurally validated before checkpointing.\n+- ID or ownership mismatches stop the batch without overwrite or renumbering.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..90fb845c6600aaad53d4748c781f372585b282e0\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0003\n+sequence: 4\n+title: Author deterministic state and connected-scope exclusion contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0002, create only `../runbooks/R0004.md` and `../runbooks/R0008.md`\n+for IMP-0004 and IMP-0008.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, the B0003/R0004/R0008 manifest records, the two\n+catalogue records, and `02-feature-model.md#domain-vocabulary-and-state-ownership`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#data-contract`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency`, and\n+`03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0004.md` \u2014 IMP-0004; dependencies R0002,R0003.\n+- `../runbooks/R0008.md` \u2014 IMP-0008; dependencies R0002,R0004.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use exact manifest provenance with `authoring_batch: B0003`, standard\n+Supervisor metadata, and `asset_impact: not_applicable` with blank\n+`asset_ids`. Each R file must include precise objective, dependencies,\n+requirements, files/data/interfaces, required behaviour, non-goals, platform\n+differences, verification/evidence, observable acceptance criteria, and an\n+`## Asset assessment` that explains no visual/source asset is needed and\n+prohibits incidental creation.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Stop on an existing conflicting R ID/path. Load both files; compare metadata,\n+provenance, dependencies, and ownership with the manifest; and verify every\n+required section before updating state.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Checkpoint B0003 only when both R files validate. Retain IDs and repair only\n+the failed output on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after R0004 and R0008; do not create services, identity, accounts, or more R files.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Exactly R0004 and R0008 are authored for their allocated IMP records.\n+- Both outputs are small, dependency-correct, fully traceable contracts with explicit no-asset assessments.\n+- Conflicting existing work stops authoring without overwrite or ID reuse.\n+- The manifest is checkpointed only after both outputs load and match it.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..2c5f4b2fd378f1ee4282e7baf11e456fbf3737d6\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0004\n+sequence: 5\n+title: Author content-validation and local recovery contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0003, create only `../runbooks/R0005.md` and `../runbooks/R0006.md`\n+for IMP-0005 and IMP-0006; retain GATE-0003.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read the B0004/R0005/R0006 manifest records, the two catalogue records,\n+`../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics`,\n+`02-feature-model.md#save-recovery-and-offline-persistence`, and\n+`04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0005.md` \u2014 IMP-0005; dependencies R0001,R0003,R0004.\n+- `../runbooks/R0006.md` \u2014 IMP-0006; dependencies R0002,R0003,R0004.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use standard front matter, exact manifest provenance (`authoring_batch: B0004`),\n+and `asset_impact: not_applicable` with blank `asset_ids`. Each output must\n+cover objective, dependencies, requirements, ownership, behaviour, non-goals,\n+platform differences, verification/evidence, observable acceptance criteria,\n+and an `## Asset assessment` forbidding incidental asset creation.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Never overwrite a conflicting R file. Load and compare both files with the\n+manifest, including provenance and dependencies, then verify required sections\n+and GATE-0003 retention.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update B0004 only after both structural checks pass; preserve IDs and repair\n+only the failed output if resumed.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after two outputs. Do not select browser storage or claim the save gate is approved.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- R0005 and R0006 are the only generated contracts and match their two IMP allocations.\n+- Both contracts retain the save/storage gate and make no incidental asset work.\n+- Loader, provenance, dependency, ownership, and required-section validation completes before checkpointing.\n+- A mismatch stops rather than overwrites an R contract.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0005.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0005.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..8db7a73ae46c480e7e5e4ec70874bd45b737b4c8\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0005.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0005\n+sequence: 6\n+title: Author migration diagnostics and provenance contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0004, create only `../runbooks/R0007.md`, `../runbooks/R0009.md`, and\n+`../runbooks/R0011.md` for IMP-0007, IMP-0009, and IMP-0011. Retain all named\n+human gates.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read the B0005/R0007/R0009/R0011 manifest records and catalogue records,\n+`../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security`,\n+`01-product-brief.md#originality-boundary`, and\n+`04-experience-contract.md#experience-premise-and-originality-boundary`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0007.md` \u2014 IMP-0007; dependencies R0005,R0006.\n+- `../runbooks/R0009.md` \u2014 IMP-0009; dependencies R0002,R0003,R0006.\n+- `../runbooks/R0011.md` \u2014 IMP-0011; dependency R0005.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use standard front matter and exact manifest provenance with `authoring_batch:\n+B0005`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`, `asset_impact: not_applicable`, and\n+blank `asset_ids`. Each small R task must provide objective, dependencies,\n+requirements, files/data/interfaces, required behaviour, non-goals, platform\n+differences, verification/evidence, observable criteria, and an `## Asset\n+assessment` prohibiting incidental asset creation.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Stop on an existing conflicting R ID/path. Load all three and compare their\n+metadata, dependencies, provenance, and ownership to the manifest; verify\n+required sections and retained GATE-0003/GATE-0005 status.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Checkpoint B0005 only after every assigned output validates. Keep accepted\n+outputs and repair only an incomplete assigned path on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after the three listed files. Do not introduce remote diagnostics, assets, or services.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Exactly R0007, R0009, and R0011 are generated for their allocated IMP records.\n+- Each R contract is bounded, traceable, dependency-correct, and has an explicit no-asset assessment.\n+- Conflicts halt without overwriting, renumbering, or assigning a replacement ID.\n+- The manifest checkpoint follows successful loader and manifest comparison only.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0006.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0006.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..cdf87c05bb005aad12679a309634f9b10c0e589b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0006.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0006\n+sequence: 7\n+title: Author the foundation documentation closure contract\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0003 and B0004, create only `../runbooks/R0012.md` for IMP-0012. It\n+documents foundation architecture/recovery boundaries without claiming product\n+implementation, approval, or release readiness.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, the B0006/R0012 manifest and catalogue records,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics`, and\n+`03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0012.md` \u2014 IMP-0012; dependencies R0002,R0004,R0006,R0008.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use standard front matter with the exact manifest provenance (`authoring_batch:\n+B0006`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`), `asset_impact: not_applicable`, and\n+blank `asset_ids`. Include objective, dependencies, requirements, ownership,\n+required behaviour, non-goals, platform differences, verification/evidence,\n+observable criteria, and an `## Asset assessment` explaining why no asset is\n+needed and prohibiting incidental assets.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Stop rather than overwrite a conflicting R0012. Load it, compare all metadata,\n+provenance, dependencies, and ownership to the manifest, and check every\n+required section and explicit retained gate.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update B0006 only after validation. Retain the reserved ID and repair only this\n+file on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after R0012; do not write a final audit or allocate another R contract.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- R0012 is the only output and maps exactly to IMP-0012.\n+- It is a bounded, loader-valid, fully traceable contract with a no-asset assessment.\n+- A conflicting existing contract is reported without overwrite or ID reuse.\n+- Checkpointing follows successful manifest comparison only.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/C0001.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/C0001.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..95e2200e33659c79dda4e2542bfa570ec224cd8c\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/C0001.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@\n+---\n+task_id: C0001\n+sequence: 1\n+title: Validate the bounded foundation catalogue bootstrap\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Validate the existing `SHARD-01` implementation catalogue before authoring.\n+Read only the canonical specification, `planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json`,\n+and `planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`. Confirm that SHARD-01 contains\n+at most 250 `IMP-*` contracts, that every ready foundation contract is allocated\n+once, and that SHARD-02 through SHARD-05 remain queued or held. Do not expand a\n+future chapter, create R-series files, or change accepted IDs.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Check unique `IMP-*`, B, and R IDs; contract-to-manifest coverage; dependency\n+closure; the 250-contract bound; and that B0001 through B0006 each contain no\n+more than seven R IDs. Record only factual repairs to the manifest/ledger when\n+the sources agree. Stop and report any missing canonical source, conflicting\n+ownership, cyclic dependency, or attempt to allocate a held connected-scope\n+chapter.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Set the manifest wave checkpoint only after the structural checks pass. Preserve\n+all counters and existing allocations; append a short checkpoint note to the\n+ledger if it does not already describe the result. Leave future allocation to\n+D0001.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- SHARD-01 is verified as a bounded catalogue of no more than 250 contracts.\n+- The twelve foundation `IMP-*` records are each allocated exactly once to B0001 through B0006, with no batch over seven R contracts.\n+- Queued and held chapters remain unexpanded and no R-series implementation runbook is created.\n+- Conflicts, missing sources, cycles, or ID collisions stop the task without renumbering or overwriting work.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..735a844029d6d1831759e0691eeaf4519fea26e1\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,73 @@\n+---\n+task_id: D0001\n+sequence: 8\n+title: Dispatch the next bounded implementation-runbook authoring wave\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Run one durable authoring-dispatch iteration after the bootstrap B0001\u2013B0006\n+wave. First expand at most one eligible queued specification/catalogue chapter\n+into no more than 250 `IMP-*` records and validate its requirement/dependency\n+coverage. Then allocate ready, unassigned contracts into at most ten new\n+B-series authoring tasks, each with at most seven R-series outputs. Create\n+exactly one successor dispatcher when a queued chapter or ready contract\n+remains; create the final audit B-series task instead only when neither exists.\n+Exit after creating that bounded set.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `INITIAL.md`, `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `../specification/README.md`,\n+`../planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json`,\n+`../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`, its Markdown ledger, and\n+`../../../runbooks/F014.md`. Read only the canonical specification sections\n+needed for the one selected chapter. Treat SHARD-05 as held unless explicit\n+authorisation is recorded; do not turn a gate into approval.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Select no more than one queued chapter whose dependencies and gates permit\n+planning. Add at most 250 stable `IMP-*` contracts with requirement links,\n+owned files/data/interfaces, dependencies, non-goals, platform distinctions,\n+verification, asset assessment, and canonical source links. Validate coverage,\n+unique IDs, ownership, and acyclic dependencies. Allocate only ready\n+unassigned contracts, using monotonic B/R counters and batches of no more than\n+seven R IDs; materialise at most ten corresponding B runbooks. Each B writer\n+must contain a context packet, output list, validation procedure,\n+checkpoint/update procedure, collision stop rule, and stop condition. Do not\n+create R-series files yourself.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Atomically update the JSON/Markdown ledger counters, chapter state, contract\n+allocations, and checkpoint after validation. Never renumber, replace, or\n+rewrite an accepted B/R contract. If work remains, create exactly one new\n+dispatcher with the next monotonic dispatcher ID and a later sequence. If no\n+queued chapter or ready contract remains, create exactly one final audit\n+B-series runbook that validates all completed catalogue expansions and batches;\n+it must not pretend to generate or review all work in this dispatch.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Validate JSON, the 250-contract chapter cap, no more than ten newly-created B\n+files, no more than seven assigned R IDs per B file, unique B/R/IMP IDs,\n+dependency closure, provenance values, asset metadata, output ownership, and\n+the successor/final-audit choice. Stop and report a source conflict, missing\n+coverage, cycle, ID/path collision, unresolved authority, or any need to\n+overwrite accepted work.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop immediately after one chapter expansion (or none), one allocation wave,\n+and exactly one successor dispatcher or final audit task. This is not a\n+recursive prompt and must not materialise a whole-game plan.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- This iteration expands at most one eligible chapter and adds no more than 250 IMP contracts.\n+- It creates at most ten bounded B-series authoring tasks, each with at most seven assigned R-series outputs.\n+- Every created B task has its context packet, output list, validation, checkpoint/update, collision protection, and stop condition.\n+- If queued or ready work remains, exactly one successor dispatcher is created; otherwise exactly one final audit B-series task is created.\n+- IDs, manifest ownership, provenance, asset assessments, and dependencies are validated without overwriting accepted work.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..5e24170a9f17243df4715c1ab64fdb1d57f52d9b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@\n+# Implementation-runbook authoring context\n+\n+This collection creates implementation instructions only. The canonical project\n+scope is [PROJECT_BRIEF.md](../PROJECT_BRIEF.md); read the canonical\n+[specification](../specification/README.md) and the allocation ledger at\n+[`../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`](../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json)\n+before writing an R-series file. Do not infer, approve, or implement unresolved\n+decisions. This collection is a child of the factory collection and its R-series\n+output is registered as its own child collection.\n+\n+The initial wave is deliberately limited to the already allocated SHARD-01\n+foundation contracts. Future work is created only by the dispatcher, one\n+catalogue chapter and at most ten B-series tasks at a time.\ndiff --git a/runbooks/.supervisor-children/mock-fantasy-quest-4.json b/runbooks/.supervisor-children/mock-fantasy-quest-4.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..06eefe3c3f6bfb75799bd665798dfd3c8424bb21\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/runbooks/.supervisor-children/mock-fantasy-quest-4.json\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\n+{\"runbooks_dir\":\"../projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks\"}\n\n succeeded in 199ms:\nloaded B0001, B0002, B0003, B0004, B0005, B0006, C0001, D0001\nchild registrations valid\nmanifest bounds and provenance valid\n?? projects/mock-fantasy-quest-2/\n?? projects/mock-fantasy-quest-3/\n?? projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/\n?? projects/mock-fantasy-quest/\n?? runbooks/.supervisor-children/\n\ncodex\n{\"status\":\"pass\",\"summary\":\"The generated collection now contains one bounded catalogue checkpoint (C0001), six manifest-backed B-series writers (B0001\u2013B0006), and one durable dispatcher (D0001). The dispatcher is explicitly capped at one 250-contract chapter and ten B tasks per iteration.\",\"changed_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/C0001.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0001.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0005.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0006.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json\",\"runbooks/.supervisor-children/mock-fantasy-quest-4.json\"],\"test_result\":\"Focused structural checks passed: all eight generated runbooks load with the Supervisor loader; both child registrations parse and resolve; manifest bounds/provenance checks pass; git diff --check passes.\",\"evidence\":{\"agent_log\":\"\",\"adapter_log\":\"\",\"test_log\":\"loaded B0001, B0002, B0003, B0004, B0005, B0006, C0001, D0001\\nchild registrations valid\\nmanifest bounds and provenance valid\",\"browser_log\":\"\",\"screenshots\":[]},\"acceptance_results\":[],\"documentation\":{\"reviewed_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/10-authoring-handoff.md\",\"supervisor/supervisor/runbooks.py\"],\"updated_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md\"],\"summary\":\"The new INITIAL context document directs writers to the canonical brief and specification.\"},\"known_limitations\":[],\"browser_coverage\":\"No browser-facing product behavior changed; this task creates authoring documents only.\",\"recommended_next_step\":\"complete\"}\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc 'PYTHONPATH=supervisor python3 -m pytest supervisor/tests/test_runbooks.py -q' in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n exited 1 in 0ms:\n/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/python3: No module named pytest\n\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..960c27ae6d9a16cbfe551f01cb096ad3a22621b3\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\n+{\"runbooks_dir\":\"../runbooks\"}\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0001.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0001.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..d44ba355dd76d32fa22b3e3bf2c7d6bb4f191032\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0001.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0001\n+sequence: 2\n+title: Author the bootstrap baseline implementation contract\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Create only `../runbooks/R0001.md` from manifest batch B0001. Its precise\n+contract is IMP-0001, \"Bootstrap reproducible shared project baseline\". It is\n+not permission to implement the game or resolve GATE-0001.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `../specification/01-product-brief.md#release-definition`,\n+`../specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability`,\n+`../planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json` (IMP-0001), and the B0001/R0001\n+manifest records. Use `../../../runbooks/TEMPLATE.md` for the Supervisor shape.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0001.md` only; metadata must use `task_id: R0001`, `sequence: 1`, `source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0001`, `authoring_batch: B0001`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`, and the manifest provenance/asset values.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Give R0001 a small, precise objective; dependencies; relevant requirement IDs;\n+owned files, data, and interfaces; required behaviour; non-goals; web/PWA\n+platform differences; verification commands and evidence; observable acceptance\n+criteria; and an `## Asset assessment` explaining that no asset is needed and\n+incidental asset creation is prohibited. Include all required standard front\n+matter, including `asset_impact: not_applicable`, blank `asset_ids`, and the\n+non-empty provenance fields exactly as the manifest records them.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Before writing, stop if R0001 exists with a different ID, catalogue mapping,\n+provenance, dependency set, or output owner. After writing, load it with\n+`supervisor.runbooks.load_task`, compare every metadata value and dependency\n+against the manifest, and confirm it has all required sections.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update only B0001's manifest state/checkpoint after successful validation.\n+Retain R0001 and its ID on any failure; repair that one path on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after R0001. Do not create another R file, choose a framework, or pass GATE-0001.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Exactly one R-series runbook, R0001, is created for the allocated IMP-0001 contract.\n+- R0001 is a bounded implementation task with the required sections, metadata, provenance, and explicit no-asset assessment.\n+- Existing conflicting R0001 content causes a stop and report rather than an overwrite.\n+- Manifest ownership and checkpoint state are updated only after structural validation passes.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..0a3720f34d5f48722a12d3de51c3ce95686cd624\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0002\n+sequence: 3\n+title: Author shared seams and deterministic harness contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Create only `../runbooks/R0002.md`, `../runbooks/R0003.md`, and\n+`../runbooks/R0010.md` for B0002. They map respectively to IMP-0002, IMP-0003,\n+and IMP-0010; B0001 must be accepted first.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, the B0002 manifest record, its three catalogue\n+records, and only these specification sections: `03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency`,\n+`04-experience-contract.md#layout-visual-tokens-and-responsive-behaviour`, and\n+`04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0002.md` \u2014 IMP-0002; dependencies R0001.\n+- `../runbooks/R0003.md` \u2014 IMP-0003; dependencies R0001,R0002.\n+- `../runbooks/R0010.md` \u2014 IMP-0010; dependencies R0001,R0002.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+For each output, use standard Supervisor front matter and the exact manifest\n+provenance (`source_specifications`, `source_catalogue_ids`, `authoring_batch:\n+B0002`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`) plus `asset_impact:\n+not_applicable` and blank `asset_ids`. Make each an individually implementable\n+task containing objective, dependencies, relevant requirements, ownership,\n+behaviour, non-goals, web/PWA differences, verification/evidence, observable\n+acceptance criteria, and an `## Asset assessment` that prohibits incidental\n+assets.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Refuse a conflicting existing R ID or path. Load every output, compare all\n+metadata and dependencies to the manifest, verify provenance fields are\n+non-empty, and verify that all three outputs have the required sections.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update only B0002's checkpoint/state after all three outputs validate. Preserve\n+accepted outputs and repair only the failed assigned file on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after these three files; do not resolve the retained design gates or write another R-series contract.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- R0002, R0003, and R0010 are the only outputs and each maps to its assigned IMP record.\n+- Each output is bounded, traceable, dependency-correct, and explicitly prohibits incidental asset work.\n+- Metadata, required sections, and manifest ownership are structurally validated before checkpointing.\n+- ID or ownership mismatches stop the batch without overwrite or renumbering.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..90fb845c6600aaad53d4748c781f372585b282e0\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0003\n+sequence: 4\n+title: Author deterministic state and connected-scope exclusion contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0002, create only `../runbooks/R0004.md` and `../runbooks/R0008.md`\n+for IMP-0004 and IMP-0008.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, the B0003/R0004/R0008 manifest records, the two\n+catalogue records, and `02-feature-model.md#domain-vocabulary-and-state-ownership`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#data-contract`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency`, and\n+`03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0004.md` \u2014 IMP-0004; dependencies R0002,R0003.\n+- `../runbooks/R0008.md` \u2014 IMP-0008; dependencies R0002,R0004.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use exact manifest provenance with `authoring_batch: B0003`, standard\n+Supervisor metadata, and `asset_impact: not_applicable` with blank\n+`asset_ids`. Each R file must include precise objective, dependencies,\n+requirements, files/data/interfaces, required behaviour, non-goals, platform\n+differences, verification/evidence, observable acceptance criteria, and an\n+`## Asset assessment` that explains no visual/source asset is needed and\n+prohibits incidental creation.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Stop on an existing conflicting R ID/path. Load both files; compare metadata,\n+provenance, dependencies, and ownership with the manifest; and verify every\n+required section before updating state.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Checkpoint B0003 only when both R files validate. Retain IDs and repair only\n+the failed output on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after R0004 and R0008; do not create services, identity, accounts, or more R files.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Exactly R0004 and R0008 are authored for their allocated IMP records.\n+- Both outputs are small, dependency-correct, fully traceable contracts with explicit no-asset assessments.\n+- Conflicting existing work stops authoring without overwrite or ID reuse.\n+- The manifest is checkpointed only after both outputs load and match it.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..2c5f4b2fd378f1ee4282e7baf11e456fbf3737d6\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0004\n+sequence: 5\n+title: Author content-validation and local recovery contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0003, create only `../runbooks/R0005.md` and `../runbooks/R0006.md`\n+for IMP-0005 and IMP-0006; retain GATE-0003.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read the B0004/R0005/R0006 manifest records, the two catalogue records,\n+`../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics`,\n+`02-feature-model.md#save-recovery-and-offline-persistence`, and\n+`04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0005.md` \u2014 IMP-0005; dependencies R0001,R0003,R0004.\n+- `../runbooks/R0006.md` \u2014 IMP-0006; dependencies R0002,R0003,R0004.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use standard front matter, exact manifest provenance (`authoring_batch: B0004`),\n+and `asset_impact: not_applicable` with blank `asset_ids`. Each output must\n+cover objective, dependencies, requirements, ownership, behaviour, non-goals,\n+platform differences, verification/evidence, observable acceptance criteria,\n+and an `## Asset assessment` forbidding incidental asset creation.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Never overwrite a conflicting R file. Load and compare both files with the\n+manifest, including provenance and dependencies, then verify required sections\n+and GATE-0003 retention.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update B0004 only after both structural checks pass; preserve IDs and repair\n+only the failed output if resumed.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after two outputs. Do not select browser storage or claim the save gate is approved.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- R0005 and R0006 are the only generated contracts and match their two IMP allocations.\n+- Both contracts retain the save/storage gate and make no incidental asset work.\n+- Loader, provenance, dependency, ownership, and required-section validation completes before checkpointing.\n+- A mismatch stops rather than overwrites an R contract.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0005.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0005.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..8db7a73ae46c480e7e5e4ec70874bd45b737b4c8\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0005.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0005\n+sequence: 6\n+title: Author migration diagnostics and provenance contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0004, create only `../runbooks/R0007.md`, `../runbooks/R0009.md`, and\n+`../runbooks/R0011.md` for IMP-0007, IMP-0009, and IMP-0011. Retain all named\n+human gates.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read the B0005/R0007/R0009/R0011 manifest records and catalogue records,\n+`../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security`,\n+`01-product-brief.md#originality-boundary`, and\n+`04-experience-contract.md#experience-premise-and-originality-boundary`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0007.md` \u2014 IMP-0007; dependencies R0005,R0006.\n+- `../runbooks/R0009.md` \u2014 IMP-0009; dependencies R0002,R0003,R0006.\n+- `../runbooks/R0011.md` \u2014 IMP-0011; dependency R0005.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use standard front matter and exact manifest provenance with `authoring_batch:\n+B0005`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`, `asset_impact: not_applicable`, and\n+blank `asset_ids`. Each small R task must provide objective, dependencies,\n+requirements, files/data/interfaces, required behaviour, non-goals, platform\n+differences, verification/evidence, observable criteria, and an `## Asset\n+assessment` prohibiting incidental asset creation.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Stop on an existing conflicting R ID/path. Load all three and compare their\n+metadata, dependencies, provenance, and ownership to the manifest; verify\n+required sections and retained GATE-0003/GATE-0005 status.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Checkpoint B0005 only after every assigned output validates. Keep accepted\n+outputs and repair only an incomplete assigned path on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after the three listed files. Do not introduce remote diagnostics, assets, or services.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Exactly R0007, R0009, and R0011 are generated for their allocated IMP records.\n+- Each R contract is bounded, traceable, dependency-correct, and has an explicit no-asset assessment.\n+- Conflicts halt without overwriting, renumbering, or assigning a replacement ID.\n+- The manifest checkpoint follows successful loader and manifest comparison only.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0006.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0006.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..cdf87c05bb005aad12679a309634f9b10c0e589b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0006.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0006\n+sequence: 7\n+title: Author the foundation documentation closure contract\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0003 and B0004, create only `../runbooks/R0012.md` for IMP-0012. It\n+documents foundation architecture/recovery boundaries without claiming product\n+implementation, approval, or release readiness.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, the B0006/R0012 manifest and catalogue records,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics`, and\n+`03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0012.md` \u2014 IMP-0012; dependencies R0002,R0004,R0006,R0008.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use standard front matter with the exact manifest provenance (`authoring_batch:\n+B0006`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`), `asset_impact: not_applicable`, and\n+blank `asset_ids`. Include objective, dependencies, requirements, ownership,\n+required behaviour, non-goals, platform differences, verification/evidence,\n+observable criteria, and an `## Asset assessment` explaining why no asset is\n+needed and prohibiting incidental assets.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Stop rather than overwrite a conflicting R0012. Load it, compare all metadata,\n+provenance, dependencies, and ownership to the manifest, and check every\n+required section and explicit retained gate.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update B0006 only after validation. Retain the reserved ID and repair only this\n+file on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after R0012; do not write a final audit or allocate another R contract.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- R0012 is the only output and maps exactly to IMP-0012.\n+- It is a bounded, loader-valid, fully traceable contract with a no-asset assessment.\n+- A conflicting existing contract is reported without overwrite or ID reuse.\n+- Checkpointing follows successful manifest comparison only.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/C0001.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/C0001.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..95e2200e33659c79dda4e2542bfa570ec224cd8c\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/C0001.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@\n+---\n+task_id: C0001\n+sequence: 1\n+title: Validate the bounded foundation catalogue bootstrap\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Validate the existing `SHARD-01` implementation catalogue before authoring.\n+Read only the canonical specification, `planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json`,\n+and `planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`. Confirm that SHARD-01 contains\n+at most 250 `IMP-*` contracts, that every ready foundation contract is allocated\n+once, and that SHARD-02 through SHARD-05 remain queued or held. Do not expand a\n+future chapter, create R-series files, or change accepted IDs.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Check unique `IMP-*`, B, and R IDs; contract-to-manifest coverage; dependency\n+closure; the 250-contract bound; and that B0001 through B0006 each contain no\n+more than seven R IDs. Record only factual repairs to the manifest/ledger when\n+the sources agree. Stop and report any missing canonical source, conflicting\n+ownership, cyclic dependency, or attempt to allocate a held connected-scope\n+chapter.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Set the manifest wave checkpoint only after the structural checks pass. Preserve\n+all counters and existing allocations; append a short checkpoint note to the\n+ledger if it does not already describe the result. Leave future allocation to\n+D0001.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- SHARD-01 is verified as a bounded catalogue of no more than 250 contracts.\n+- The twelve foundation `IMP-*` records are each allocated exactly once to B0001 through B0006, with no batch over seven R contracts.\n+- Queued and held chapters remain unexpanded and no R-series implementation runbook is created.\n+- Conflicts, missing sources, cycles, or ID collisions stop the task without renumbering or overwriting work.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..735a844029d6d1831759e0691eeaf4519fea26e1\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,73 @@\n+---\n+task_id: D0001\n+sequence: 8\n+title: Dispatch the next bounded implementation-runbook authoring wave\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Run one durable authoring-dispatch iteration after the bootstrap B0001\u2013B0006\n+wave. First expand at most one eligible queued specification/catalogue chapter\n+into no more than 250 `IMP-*` records and validate its requirement/dependency\n+coverage. Then allocate ready, unassigned contracts into at most ten new\n+B-series authoring tasks, each with at most seven R-series outputs. Create\n+exactly one successor dispatcher when a queued chapter or ready contract\n+remains; create the final audit B-series task instead only when neither exists.\n+Exit after creating that bounded set.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `INITIAL.md`, `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `../specification/README.md`,\n+`../planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json`,\n+`../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`, its Markdown ledger, and\n+`../../../runbooks/F014.md`. Read only the canonical specification sections\n+needed for the one selected chapter. Treat SHARD-05 as held unless explicit\n+authorisation is recorded; do not turn a gate into approval.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Select no more than one queued chapter whose dependencies and gates permit\n+planning. Add at most 250 stable `IMP-*` contracts with requirement links,\n+owned files/data/interfaces, dependencies, non-goals, platform distinctions,\n+verification, asset assessment, and canonical source links. Validate coverage,\n+unique IDs, ownership, and acyclic dependencies. Allocate only ready\n+unassigned contracts, using monotonic B/R counters and batches of no more than\n+seven R IDs; materialise at most ten corresponding B runbooks. Each B writer\n+must contain a context packet, output list, validation procedure,\n+checkpoint/update procedure, collision stop rule, and stop condition. Do not\n+create R-series files yourself.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Atomically update the JSON/Markdown ledger counters, chapter state, contract\n+allocations, and checkpoint after validation. Never renumber, replace, or\n+rewrite an accepted B/R contract. If work remains, create exactly one new\n+dispatcher with the next monotonic dispatcher ID and a later sequence. If no\n+queued chapter or ready contract remains, create exactly one final audit\n+B-series runbook that validates all completed catalogue expansions and batches;\n+it must not pretend to generate or review all work in this dispatch.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Validate JSON, the 250-contract chapter cap, no more than ten newly-created B\n+files, no more than seven assigned R IDs per B file, unique B/R/IMP IDs,\n+dependency closure, provenance values, asset metadata, output ownership, and\n+the successor/final-audit choice. Stop and report a source conflict, missing\n+coverage, cycle, ID/path collision, unresolved authority, or any need to\n+overwrite accepted work.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop immediately after one chapter expansion (or none), one allocation wave,\n+and exactly one successor dispatcher or final audit task. This is not a\n+recursive prompt and must not materialise a whole-game plan.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- This iteration expands at most one eligible chapter and adds no more than 250 IMP contracts.\n+- It creates at most ten bounded B-series authoring tasks, each with at most seven assigned R-series outputs.\n+- Every created B task has its context packet, output list, validation, checkpoint/update, collision protection, and stop condition.\n+- If queued or ready work remains, exactly one successor dispatcher is created; otherwise exactly one final audit B-series task is created.\n+- IDs, manifest ownership, provenance, asset assessments, and dependencies are validated without overwriting accepted work.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..5e24170a9f17243df4715c1ab64fdb1d57f52d9b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@\n+# Implementation-runbook authoring context\n+\n+This collection creates implementation instructions only. The canonical project\n+scope is [PROJECT_BRIEF.md](../PROJECT_BRIEF.md); read the canonical\n+[specification](../specification/README.md) and the allocation ledger at\n+[`../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`](../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json)\n+before writing an R-series file. Do not infer, approve, or implement unresolved\n+decisions. This collection is a child of the factory collection and its R-series\n+output is registered as its own child collection.\n+\n+The initial wave is deliberately limited to the already allocated SHARD-01\n+foundation contracts. Future work is created only by the dispatcher, one\n+catalogue chapter and at most ten B-series tasks at a time.\ndiff --git a/runbooks/.supervisor-children/mock-fantasy-quest-4.json b/runbooks/.supervisor-children/mock-fantasy-quest-4.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..06eefe3c3f6bfb75799bd665798dfd3c8424bb21\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/runbooks/.supervisor-children/mock-fantasy-quest-4.json\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\n+{\"runbooks_dir\":\"../projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks\"}\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,120p' supervisor/pyproject.toml; find supervisor -maxdepth 2 -type d -name '.venv' -print; git diff --check\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=68\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\n[project]\nname = \"runbook-supervisor\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"Evidence-gated LangGraph task supervisor.\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.10\"\ndependencies = [\n  \"langgraph>=1.2,<2\",\n  \"opentelemetry-api>=1.28,<2\",\n  \"opentelemetry-sdk>=1.28,<2\",\n  \"opentelemetry-exporter-otlp-proto-http>=1.28,<2\",\n  \"pydantic>=2.7,<3\",\n  \"python-dotenv>=1.0,<2\",\n]\n\n[project.optional-dependencies]\ndev = [\"pytest>=8,<9\"]\n\n[project.scripts]\nsupervisor-run = \"supervisor.cli:main\"\nsupervisor-reports = \"supervisor.reports_cli:main\"\nsupervisor-dashboard = \"supervisor.dashboard:main\"\nsupervisor-observability-import = \"supervisor.observability_import:main\"\nsupervisor = \"supervisor.manage:main\"\n\n[tool.setuptools.packages.find]\ninclude = [\"supervisor*\"]\n\n[tool.setuptools.package-data]\nsupervisor = [\"env_migrations.json\"]\n\n[tool.pytest.ini_options]\ntestpaths = [\"tests\"]\npythonpath = [\".\"]\nsupervisor/.venv\n\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..960c27ae6d9a16cbfe551f01cb096ad3a22621b3\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\n+{\"runbooks_dir\":\"../runbooks\"}\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0001.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0001.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..d44ba355dd76d32fa22b3e3bf2c7d6bb4f191032\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0001.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0001\n+sequence: 2\n+title: Author the bootstrap baseline implementation contract\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Create only `../runbooks/R0001.md` from manifest batch B0001. Its precise\n+contract is IMP-0001, \"Bootstrap reproducible shared project baseline\". It is\n+not permission to implement the game or resolve GATE-0001.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `../specification/01-product-brief.md#release-definition`,\n+`../specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability`,\n+`../planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json` (IMP-0001), and the B0001/R0001\n+manifest records. Use `../../../runbooks/TEMPLATE.md` for the Supervisor shape.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0001.md` only; metadata must use `task_id: R0001`, `sequence: 1`, `source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0001`, `authoring_batch: B0001`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`, and the manifest provenance/asset values.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Give R0001 a small, precise objective; dependencies; relevant requirement IDs;\n+owned files, data, and interfaces; required behaviour; non-goals; web/PWA\n+platform differences; verification commands and evidence; observable acceptance\n+criteria; and an `## Asset assessment` explaining that no asset is needed and\n+incidental asset creation is prohibited. Include all required standard front\n+matter, including `asset_impact: not_applicable`, blank `asset_ids`, and the\n+non-empty provenance fields exactly as the manifest records them.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Before writing, stop if R0001 exists with a different ID, catalogue mapping,\n+provenance, dependency set, or output owner. After writing, load it with\n+`supervisor.runbooks.load_task`, compare every metadata value and dependency\n+against the manifest, and confirm it has all required sections.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update only B0001's manifest state/checkpoint after successful validation.\n+Retain R0001 and its ID on any failure; repair that one path on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after R0001. Do not create another R file, choose a framework, or pass GATE-0001.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Exactly one R-series runbook, R0001, is created for the allocated IMP-0001 contract.\n+- R0001 is a bounded implementation task with the required sections, metadata, provenance, and explicit no-asset assessment.\n+- Existing conflicting R0001 content causes a stop and report rather than an overwrite.\n+- Manifest ownership and checkpoint state are updated only after structural validation passes.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..0a3720f34d5f48722a12d3de51c3ce95686cd624\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0002\n+sequence: 3\n+title: Author shared seams and deterministic harness contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Create only `../runbooks/R0002.md`, `../runbooks/R0003.md`, and\n+`../runbooks/R0010.md` for B0002. They map respectively to IMP-0002, IMP-0003,\n+and IMP-0010; B0001 must be accepted first.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, the B0002 manifest record, its three catalogue\n+records, and only these specification sections: `03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency`,\n+`04-experience-contract.md#layout-visual-tokens-and-responsive-behaviour`, and\n+`04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0002.md` \u2014 IMP-0002; dependencies R0001.\n+- `../runbooks/R0003.md` \u2014 IMP-0003; dependencies R0001,R0002.\n+- `../runbooks/R0010.md` \u2014 IMP-0010; dependencies R0001,R0002.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+For each output, use standard Supervisor front matter and the exact manifest\n+provenance (`source_specifications`, `source_catalogue_ids`, `authoring_batch:\n+B0002`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`) plus `asset_impact:\n+not_applicable` and blank `asset_ids`. Make each an individually implementable\n+task containing objective, dependencies, relevant requirements, ownership,\n+behaviour, non-goals, web/PWA differences, verification/evidence, observable\n+acceptance criteria, and an `## Asset assessment` that prohibits incidental\n+assets.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Refuse a conflicting existing R ID or path. Load every output, compare all\n+metadata and dependencies to the manifest, verify provenance fields are\n+non-empty, and verify that all three outputs have the required sections.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update only B0002's checkpoint/state after all three outputs validate. Preserve\n+accepted outputs and repair only the failed assigned file on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after these three files; do not resolve the retained design gates or write another R-series contract.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- R0002, R0003, and R0010 are the only outputs and each maps to its assigned IMP record.\n+- Each output is bounded, traceable, dependency-correct, and explicitly prohibits incidental asset work.\n+- Metadata, required sections, and manifest ownership are structurally validated before checkpointing.\n+- ID or ownership mismatches stop the batch without overwrite or renumbering.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..90fb845c6600aaad53d4748c781f372585b282e0\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0003\n+sequence: 4\n+title: Author deterministic state and connected-scope exclusion contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0002, create only `../runbooks/R0004.md` and `../runbooks/R0008.md`\n+for IMP-0004 and IMP-0008.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, the B0003/R0004/R0008 manifest records, the two\n+catalogue records, and `02-feature-model.md#domain-vocabulary-and-state-ownership`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#data-contract`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency`, and\n+`03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0004.md` \u2014 IMP-0004; dependencies R0002,R0003.\n+- `../runbooks/R0008.md` \u2014 IMP-0008; dependencies R0002,R0004.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use exact manifest provenance with `authoring_batch: B0003`, standard\n+Supervisor metadata, and `asset_impact: not_applicable` with blank\n+`asset_ids`. Each R file must include precise objective, dependencies,\n+requirements, files/data/interfaces, required behaviour, non-goals, platform\n+differences, verification/evidence, observable acceptance criteria, and an\n+`## Asset assessment` that explains no visual/source asset is needed and\n+prohibits incidental creation.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Stop on an existing conflicting R ID/path. Load both files; compare metadata,\n+provenance, dependencies, and ownership with the manifest; and verify every\n+required section before updating state.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Checkpoint B0003 only when both R files validate. Retain IDs and repair only\n+the failed output on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after R0004 and R0008; do not create services, identity, accounts, or more R files.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Exactly R0004 and R0008 are authored for their allocated IMP records.\n+- Both outputs are small, dependency-correct, fully traceable contracts with explicit no-asset assessments.\n+- Conflicting existing work stops authoring without overwrite or ID reuse.\n+- The manifest is checkpointed only after both outputs load and match it.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..2c5f4b2fd378f1ee4282e7baf11e456fbf3737d6\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0004\n+sequence: 5\n+title: Author content-validation and local recovery contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0003, create only `../runbooks/R0005.md` and `../runbooks/R0006.md`\n+for IMP-0005 and IMP-0006; retain GATE-0003.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read the B0004/R0005/R0006 manifest records, the two catalogue records,\n+`../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics`,\n+`02-feature-model.md#save-recovery-and-offline-persistence`, and\n+`04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0005.md` \u2014 IMP-0005; dependencies R0001,R0003,R0004.\n+- `../runbooks/R0006.md` \u2014 IMP-0006; dependencies R0002,R0003,R0004.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use standard front matter, exact manifest provenance (`authoring_batch: B0004`),\n+and `asset_impact: not_applicable` with blank `asset_ids`. Each output must\n+cover objective, dependencies, requirements, ownership, behaviour, non-goals,\n+platform differences, verification/evidence, observable acceptance criteria,\n+and an `## Asset assessment` forbidding incidental asset creation.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Never overwrite a conflicting R file. Load and compare both files with the\n+manifest, including provenance and dependencies, then verify required sections\n+and GATE-0003 retention.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update B0004 only after both structural checks pass; preserve IDs and repair\n+only the failed output if resumed.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after two outputs. Do not select browser storage or claim the save gate is approved.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- R0005 and R0006 are the only generated contracts and match their two IMP allocations.\n+- Both contracts retain the save/storage gate and make no incidental asset work.\n+- Loader, provenance, dependency, ownership, and required-section validation completes before checkpointing.\n+- A mismatch stops rather than overwrites an R contract.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0005.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0005.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..8db7a73ae46c480e7e5e4ec70874bd45b737b4c8\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0005.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0005\n+sequence: 6\n+title: Author migration diagnostics and provenance contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0004, create only `../runbooks/R0007.md`, `../runbooks/R0009.md`, and\n+`../runbooks/R0011.md` for IMP-0007, IMP-0009, and IMP-0011. Retain all named\n+human gates.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read the B0005/R0007/R0009/R0011 manifest records and catalogue records,\n+`../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security`,\n+`01-product-brief.md#originality-boundary`, and\n+`04-experience-contract.md#experience-premise-and-originality-boundary`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0007.md` \u2014 IMP-0007; dependencies R0005,R0006.\n+- `../runbooks/R0009.md` \u2014 IMP-0009; dependencies R0002,R0003,R0006.\n+- `../runbooks/R0011.md` \u2014 IMP-0011; dependency R0005.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use standard front matter and exact manifest provenance with `authoring_batch:\n+B0005`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`, `asset_impact: not_applicable`, and\n+blank `asset_ids`. Each small R task must provide objective, dependencies,\n+requirements, files/data/interfaces, required behaviour, non-goals, platform\n+differences, verification/evidence, observable criteria, and an `## Asset\n+assessment` prohibiting incidental asset creation.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Stop on an existing conflicting R ID/path. Load all three and compare their\n+metadata, dependencies, provenance, and ownership to the manifest; verify\n+required sections and retained GATE-0003/GATE-0005 status.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Checkpoint B0005 only after every assigned output validates. Keep accepted\n+outputs and repair only an incomplete assigned path on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after the three listed files. Do not introduce remote diagnostics, assets, or services.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Exactly R0007, R0009, and R0011 are generated for their allocated IMP records.\n+- Each R contract is bounded, traceable, dependency-correct, and has an explicit no-asset assessment.\n+- Conflicts halt without overwriting, renumbering, or assigning a replacement ID.\n+- The manifest checkpoint follows successful loader and manifest comparison only.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0006.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0006.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..cdf87c05bb005aad12679a309634f9b10c0e589b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0006.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0006\n+sequence: 7\n+title: Author the foundation documentation closure contract\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0003 and B0004, create only `../runbooks/R0012.md` for IMP-0012. It\n+documents foundation architecture/recovery boundaries without claiming product\n+implementation, approval, or release readiness.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, the B0006/R0012 manifest and catalogue records,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics`, and\n+`03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0012.md` \u2014 IMP-0012; dependencies R0002,R0004,R0006,R0008.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use standard front matter with the exact manifest provenance (`authoring_batch:\n+B0006`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`), `asset_impact: not_applicable`, and\n+blank `asset_ids`. Include objective, dependencies, requirements, ownership,\n+required behaviour, non-goals, platform differences, verification/evidence,\n+observable criteria, and an `## Asset assessment` explaining why no asset is\n+needed and prohibiting incidental assets.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Stop rather than overwrite a conflicting R0012. Load it, compare all metadata,\n+provenance, dependencies, and ownership to the manifest, and check every\n+required section and explicit retained gate.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update B0006 only after validation. Retain the reserved ID and repair only this\n+file on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after R0012; do not write a final audit or allocate another R contract.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- R0012 is the only output and maps exactly to IMP-0012.\n+- It is a bounded, loader-valid, fully traceable contract with a no-asset assessment.\n+- A conflicting existing contract is reported without overwrite or ID reuse.\n+- Checkpointing follows successful manifest comparison only.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/C0001.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/C0001.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..95e2200e33659c79dda4e2542bfa570ec224cd8c\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/C0001.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@\n+---\n+task_id: C0001\n+sequence: 1\n+title: Validate the bounded foundation catalogue bootstrap\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Validate the existing `SHARD-01` implementation catalogue before authoring.\n+Read only the canonical specification, `planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json`,\n+and `planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`. Confirm that SHARD-01 contains\n+at most 250 `IMP-*` contracts, that every ready foundation contract is allocated\n+once, and that SHARD-02 through SHARD-05 remain queued or held. Do not expand a\n+future chapter, create R-series files, or change accepted IDs.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Check unique `IMP-*`, B, and R IDs; contract-to-manifest coverage; dependency\n+closure; the 250-contract bound; and that B0001 through B0006 each contain no\n+more than seven R IDs. Record only factual repairs to the manifest/ledger when\n+the sources agree. Stop and report any missing canonical source, conflicting\n+ownership, cyclic dependency, or attempt to allocate a held connected-scope\n+chapter.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Set the manifest wave checkpoint only after the structural checks pass. Preserve\n+all counters and existing allocations; append a short checkpoint note to the\n+ledger if it does not already describe the result. Leave future allocation to\n+D0001.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- SHARD-01 is verified as a bounded catalogue of no more than 250 contracts.\n+- The twelve foundation `IMP-*` records are each allocated exactly once to B0001 through B0006, with no batch over seven R contracts.\n+- Queued and held chapters remain unexpanded and no R-series implementation runbook is created.\n+- Conflicts, missing sources, cycles, or ID collisions stop the task without renumbering or overwriting work.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..735a844029d6d1831759e0691eeaf4519fea26e1\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,73 @@\n+---\n+task_id: D0001\n+sequence: 8\n+title: Dispatch the next bounded implementation-runbook authoring wave\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Run one durable authoring-dispatch iteration after the bootstrap B0001\u2013B0006\n+wave. First expand at most one eligible queued specification/catalogue chapter\n+into no more than 250 `IMP-*` records and validate its requirement/dependency\n+coverage. Then allocate ready, unassigned contracts into at most ten new\n+B-series authoring tasks, each with at most seven R-series outputs. Create\n+exactly one successor dispatcher when a queued chapter or ready contract\n+remains; create the final audit B-series task instead only when neither exists.\n+Exit after creating that bounded set.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `INITIAL.md`, `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `../specification/README.md`,\n+`../planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json`,\n+`../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`, its Markdown ledger, and\n+`../../../runbooks/F014.md`. Read only the canonical specification sections\n+needed for the one selected chapter. Treat SHARD-05 as held unless explicit\n+authorisation is recorded; do not turn a gate into approval.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Select no more than one queued chapter whose dependencies and gates permit\n+planning. Add at most 250 stable `IMP-*` contracts with requirement links,\n+owned files/data/interfaces, dependencies, non-goals, platform distinctions,\n+verification, asset assessment, and canonical source links. Validate coverage,\n+unique IDs, ownership, and acyclic dependencies. Allocate only ready\n+unassigned contracts, using monotonic B/R counters and batches of no more than\n+seven R IDs; materialise at most ten corresponding B runbooks. Each B writer\n+must contain a context packet, output list, validation procedure,\n+checkpoint/update procedure, collision stop rule, and stop condition. Do not\n+create R-series files yourself.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Atomically update the JSON/Markdown ledger counters, chapter state, contract\n+allocations, and checkpoint after validation. Never renumber, replace, or\n+rewrite an accepted B/R contract. If work remains, create exactly one new\n+dispatcher with the next monotonic dispatcher ID and a later sequence. If no\n+queued chapter or ready contract remains, create exactly one final audit\n+B-series runbook that validates all completed catalogue expansions and batches;\n+it must not pretend to generate or review all work in this dispatch.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Validate JSON, the 250-contract chapter cap, no more than ten newly-created B\n+files, no more than seven assigned R IDs per B file, unique B/R/IMP IDs,\n+dependency closure, provenance values, asset metadata, output ownership, and\n+the successor/final-audit choice. Stop and report a source conflict, missing\n+coverage, cycle, ID/path collision, unresolved authority, or any need to\n+overwrite accepted work.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop immediately after one chapter expansion (or none), one allocation wave,\n+and exactly one successor dispatcher or final audit task. This is not a\n+recursive prompt and must not materialise a whole-game plan.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- This iteration expands at most one eligible chapter and adds no more than 250 IMP contracts.\n+- It creates at most ten bounded B-series authoring tasks, each with at most seven assigned R-series outputs.\n+- Every created B task has its context packet, output list, validation, checkpoint/update, collision protection, and stop condition.\n+- If queued or ready work remains, exactly one successor dispatcher is created; otherwise exactly one final audit B-series task is created.\n+- IDs, manifest ownership, provenance, asset assessments, and dependencies are validated without overwriting accepted work.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..5e24170a9f17243df4715c1ab64fdb1d57f52d9b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@\n+# Implementation-runbook authoring context\n+\n+This collection creates implementation instructions only. The canonical project\n+scope is [PROJECT_BRIEF.md](../PROJECT_BRIEF.md); read the canonical\n+[specification](../specification/README.md) and the allocation ledger at\n+[`../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`](../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json)\n+before writing an R-series file. Do not infer, approve, or implement unresolved\n+decisions. This collection is a child of the factory collection and its R-series\n+output is registered as its own child collection.\n+\n+The initial wave is deliberately limited to the already allocated SHARD-01\n+foundation contracts. Future work is created only by the dispatcher, one\n+catalogue chapter and at most ten B-series tasks at a time.\ndiff --git a/runbooks/.supervisor-children/mock-fantasy-quest-4.json b/runbooks/.supervisor-children/mock-fantasy-quest-4.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..06eefe3c3f6bfb75799bd665798dfd3c8424bb21\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/runbooks/.supervisor-children/mock-fantasy-quest-4.json\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\n+{\"runbooks_dir\":\"../projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks\"}\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc 'PYTHONPATH=supervisor supervisor/.venv/bin/python -m pytest supervisor/tests/test_runbooks.py -q' in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..960c27ae6d9a16cbfe551f01cb096ad3a22621b3\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\n+{\"runbooks_dir\":\"../runbooks\"}\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0001.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0001.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..d44ba355dd76d32fa22b3e3bf2c7d6bb4f191032\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0001.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0001\n+sequence: 2\n+title: Author the bootstrap baseline implementation contract\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Create only `../runbooks/R0001.md` from manifest batch B0001. Its precise\n+contract is IMP-0001, \"Bootstrap reproducible shared project baseline\". It is\n+not permission to implement the game or resolve GATE-0001.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `../specification/01-product-brief.md#release-definition`,\n+`../specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability`,\n+`../planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json` (IMP-0001), and the B0001/R0001\n+manifest records. Use `../../../runbooks/TEMPLATE.md` for the Supervisor shape.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0001.md` only; metadata must use `task_id: R0001`, `sequence: 1`, `source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0001`, `authoring_batch: B0001`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`, and the manifest provenance/asset values.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Give R0001 a small, precise objective; dependencies; relevant requirement IDs;\n+owned files, data, and interfaces; required behaviour; non-goals; web/PWA\n+platform differences; verification commands and evidence; observable acceptance\n+criteria; and an `## Asset assessment` explaining that no asset is needed and\n+incidental asset creation is prohibited. Include all required standard front\n+matter, including `asset_impact: not_applicable`, blank `asset_ids`, and the\n+non-empty provenance fields exactly as the manifest records them.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Before writing, stop if R0001 exists with a different ID, catalogue mapping,\n+provenance, dependency set, or output owner. After writing, load it with\n+`supervisor.runbooks.load_task`, compare every metadata value and dependency\n+against the manifest, and confirm it has all required sections.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update only B0001's manifest state/checkpoint after successful validation.\n+Retain R0001 and its ID on any failure; repair that one path on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after R0001. Do not create another R file, choose a framework, or pass GATE-0001.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Exactly one R-series runbook, R0001, is created for the allocated IMP-0001 contract.\n+- R0001 is a bounded implementation task with the required sections, metadata, provenance, and explicit no-asset assessment.\n+- Existing conflicting R0001 content causes a stop and report rather than an overwrite.\n+- Manifest ownership and checkpoint state are updated only after structural validation passes.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..0a3720f34d5f48722a12d3de51c3ce95686cd624\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0002\n+sequence: 3\n+title: Author shared seams and deterministic harness contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Create only `../runbooks/R0002.md`, `../runbooks/R0003.md`, and\n+`../runbooks/R0010.md` for B0002. They map respectively to IMP-0002, IMP-0003,\n+and IMP-0010; B0001 must be accepted first.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, the B0002 manifest record, its three catalogue\n+records, and only these specification sections: `03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency`,\n+`04-experience-contract.md#layout-visual-tokens-and-responsive-behaviour`, and\n+`04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0002.md` \u2014 IMP-0002; dependencies R0001.\n+- `../runbooks/R0003.md` \u2014 IMP-0003; dependencies R0001,R0002.\n+- `../runbooks/R0010.md` \u2014 IMP-0010; dependencies R0001,R0002.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+For each output, use standard Supervisor front matter and the exact manifest\n+provenance (`source_specifications`, `source_catalogue_ids`, `authoring_batch:\n+B0002`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`) plus `asset_impact:\n+not_applicable` and blank `asset_ids`. Make each an individually implementable\n+task containing objective, dependencies, relevant requirements, ownership,\n+behaviour, non-goals, web/PWA differences, verification/evidence, observable\n+acceptance criteria, and an `## Asset assessment` that prohibits incidental\n+assets.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Refuse a conflicting existing R ID or path. Load every output, compare all\n+metadata and dependencies to the manifest, verify provenance fields are\n+non-empty, and verify that all three outputs have the required sections.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update only B0002's checkpoint/state after all three outputs validate. Preserve\n+accepted outputs and repair only the failed assigned file on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after these three files; do not resolve the retained design gates or write another R-series contract.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- R0002, R0003, and R0010 are the only outputs and each maps to its assigned IMP record.\n+- Each output is bounded, traceable, dependency-correct, and explicitly prohibits incidental asset work.\n+- Metadata, required sections, and manifest ownership are structurally validated before checkpointing.\n+- ID or ownership mismatches stop the batch without overwrite or renumbering.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..90fb845c6600aaad53d4748c781f372585b282e0\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0003\n+sequence: 4\n+title: Author deterministic state and connected-scope exclusion contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0002, create only `../runbooks/R0004.md` and `../runbooks/R0008.md`\n+for IMP-0004 and IMP-0008.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, the B0003/R0004/R0008 manifest records, the two\n+catalogue records, and `02-feature-model.md#domain-vocabulary-and-state-ownership`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#data-contract`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency`, and\n+`03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0004.md` \u2014 IMP-0004; dependencies R0002,R0003.\n+- `../runbooks/R0008.md` \u2014 IMP-0008; dependencies R0002,R0004.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use exact manifest provenance with `authoring_batch: B0003`, standard\n+Supervisor metadata, and `asset_impact: not_applicable` with blank\n+`asset_ids`. Each R file must include precise objective, dependencies,\n+requirements, files/data/interfaces, required behaviour, non-goals, platform\n+differences, verification/evidence, observable acceptance criteria, and an\n+`## Asset assessment` that explains no visual/source asset is needed and\n+prohibits incidental creation.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Stop on an existing conflicting R ID/path. Load both files; compare metadata,\n+provenance, dependencies, and ownership with the manifest; and verify every\n+required section before updating state.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Checkpoint B0003 only when both R files validate. Retain IDs and repair only\n+the failed output on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after R0004 and R0008; do not create services, identity, accounts, or more R files.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Exactly R0004 and R0008 are authored for their allocated IMP records.\n+- Both outputs are small, dependency-correct, fully traceable contracts with explicit no-asset assessments.\n+- Conflicting existing work stops authoring without overwrite or ID reuse.\n+- The manifest is checkpointed only after both outputs load and match it.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..2c5f4b2fd378f1ee4282e7baf11e456fbf3737d6\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0004\n+sequence: 5\n+title: Author content-validation and local recovery contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0003, create only `../runbooks/R0005.md` and `../runbooks/R0006.md`\n+for IMP-0005 and IMP-0006; retain GATE-0003.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read the B0004/R0005/R0006 manifest records, the two catalogue records,\n+`../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics`,\n+`02-feature-model.md#save-recovery-and-offline-persistence`, and\n+`04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0005.md` \u2014 IMP-0005; dependencies R0001,R0003,R0004.\n+- `../runbooks/R0006.md` \u2014 IMP-0006; dependencies R0002,R0003,R0004.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use standard front matter, exact manifest provenance (`authoring_batch: B0004`),\n+and `asset_impact: not_applicable` with blank `asset_ids`. Each output must\n+cover objective, dependencies, requirements, ownership, behaviour, non-goals,\n+platform differences, verification/evidence, observable acceptance criteria,\n+and an `## Asset assessment` forbidding incidental asset creation.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Never overwrite a conflicting R file. Load and compare both files with the\n+manifest, including provenance and dependencies, then verify required sections\n+and GATE-0003 retention.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update B0004 only after both structural checks pass; preserve IDs and repair\n+only the failed output if resumed.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after two outputs. Do not select browser storage or claim the save gate is approved.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- R0005 and R0006 are the only generated contracts and match their two IMP allocations.\n+- Both contracts retain the save/storage gate and make no incidental asset work.\n+- Loader, provenance, dependency, ownership, and required-section validation completes before checkpointing.\n+- A mismatch stops rather than overwrites an R contract.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0005.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0005.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..8db7a73ae46c480e7e5e4ec70874bd45b737b4c8\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0005.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0005\n+sequence: 6\n+title: Author migration diagnostics and provenance contracts\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0004, create only `../runbooks/R0007.md`, `../runbooks/R0009.md`, and\n+`../runbooks/R0011.md` for IMP-0007, IMP-0009, and IMP-0011. Retain all named\n+human gates.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read the B0005/R0007/R0009/R0011 manifest records and catalogue records,\n+`../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security`,\n+`01-product-brief.md#originality-boundary`, and\n+`04-experience-contract.md#experience-premise-and-originality-boundary`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0007.md` \u2014 IMP-0007; dependencies R0005,R0006.\n+- `../runbooks/R0009.md` \u2014 IMP-0009; dependencies R0002,R0003,R0006.\n+- `../runbooks/R0011.md` \u2014 IMP-0011; dependency R0005.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use standard front matter and exact manifest provenance with `authoring_batch:\n+B0005`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`, `asset_impact: not_applicable`, and\n+blank `asset_ids`. Each small R task must provide objective, dependencies,\n+requirements, files/data/interfaces, required behaviour, non-goals, platform\n+differences, verification/evidence, observable criteria, and an `## Asset\n+assessment` prohibiting incidental asset creation.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Stop on an existing conflicting R ID/path. Load all three and compare their\n+metadata, dependencies, provenance, and ownership to the manifest; verify\n+required sections and retained GATE-0003/GATE-0005 status.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Checkpoint B0005 only after every assigned output validates. Keep accepted\n+outputs and repair only an incomplete assigned path on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after the three listed files. Do not introduce remote diagnostics, assets, or services.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Exactly R0007, R0009, and R0011 are generated for their allocated IMP records.\n+- Each R contract is bounded, traceable, dependency-correct, and has an explicit no-asset assessment.\n+- Conflicts halt without overwriting, renumbering, or assigning a replacement ID.\n+- The manifest checkpoint follows successful loader and manifest comparison only.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0006.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0006.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..cdf87c05bb005aad12679a309634f9b10c0e589b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0006.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@\n+---\n+task_id: B0006\n+sequence: 7\n+title: Author the foundation documentation closure contract\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After B0003 and B0004, create only `../runbooks/R0012.md` for IMP-0012. It\n+documents foundation architecture/recovery boundaries without claiming product\n+implementation, approval, or release readiness.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, the B0006/R0012 manifest and catalogue records,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability`,\n+`03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics`, and\n+`03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security`.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- `../runbooks/R0012.md` \u2014 IMP-0012; dependencies R0002,R0004,R0006,R0008.\n+\n+## Required authoring content\n+\n+Use standard front matter with the exact manifest provenance (`authoring_batch:\n+B0006`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`), `asset_impact: not_applicable`, and\n+blank `asset_ids`. Include objective, dependencies, requirements, ownership,\n+required behaviour, non-goals, platform differences, verification/evidence,\n+observable criteria, and an `## Asset assessment` explaining why no asset is\n+needed and prohibiting incidental assets.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Stop rather than overwrite a conflicting R0012. Load it, compare all metadata,\n+provenance, dependencies, and ownership to the manifest, and check every\n+required section and explicit retained gate.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Update B0006 only after validation. Retain the reserved ID and repair only this\n+file on resume.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop after R0012; do not write a final audit or allocate another R contract.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- R0012 is the only output and maps exactly to IMP-0012.\n+- It is a bounded, loader-valid, fully traceable contract with a no-asset assessment.\n+- A conflicting existing contract is reported without overwrite or ID reuse.\n+- Checkpointing follows successful manifest comparison only.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/C0001.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/C0001.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..95e2200e33659c79dda4e2542bfa570ec224cd8c\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/C0001.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@\n+---\n+task_id: C0001\n+sequence: 1\n+title: Validate the bounded foundation catalogue bootstrap\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Validate the existing `SHARD-01` implementation catalogue before authoring.\n+Read only the canonical specification, `planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json`,\n+and `planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`. Confirm that SHARD-01 contains\n+at most 250 `IMP-*` contracts, that every ready foundation contract is allocated\n+once, and that SHARD-02 through SHARD-05 remain queued or held. Do not expand a\n+future chapter, create R-series files, or change accepted IDs.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Check unique `IMP-*`, B, and R IDs; contract-to-manifest coverage; dependency\n+closure; the 250-contract bound; and that B0001 through B0006 each contain no\n+more than seven R IDs. Record only factual repairs to the manifest/ledger when\n+the sources agree. Stop and report any missing canonical source, conflicting\n+ownership, cyclic dependency, or attempt to allocate a held connected-scope\n+chapter.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Set the manifest wave checkpoint only after the structural checks pass. Preserve\n+all counters and existing allocations; append a short checkpoint note to the\n+ledger if it does not already describe the result. Leave future allocation to\n+D0001.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- SHARD-01 is verified as a bounded catalogue of no more than 250 contracts.\n+- The twelve foundation `IMP-*` records are each allocated exactly once to B0001 through B0006, with no batch over seven R contracts.\n+- Queued and held chapters remain unexpanded and no R-series implementation runbook is created.\n+- Conflicts, missing sources, cycles, or ID collisions stop the task without renumbering or overwriting work.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..735a844029d6d1831759e0691eeaf4519fea26e1\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,73 @@\n+---\n+task_id: D0001\n+sequence: 8\n+title: Dispatch the next bounded implementation-runbook authoring wave\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Run one durable authoring-dispatch iteration after the bootstrap B0001\u2013B0006\n+wave. First expand at most one eligible queued specification/catalogue chapter\n+into no more than 250 `IMP-*` records and validate its requirement/dependency\n+coverage. Then allocate ready, unassigned contracts into at most ten new\n+B-series authoring tasks, each with at most seven R-series outputs. Create\n+exactly one successor dispatcher when a queued chapter or ready contract\n+remains; create the final audit B-series task instead only when neither exists.\n+Exit after creating that bounded set.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `INITIAL.md`, `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `../specification/README.md`,\n+`../planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json`,\n+`../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`, its Markdown ledger, and\n+`../../../runbooks/F014.md`. Read only the canonical specification sections\n+needed for the one selected chapter. Treat SHARD-05 as held unless explicit\n+authorisation is recorded; do not turn a gate into approval.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Select no more than one queued chapter whose dependencies and gates permit\n+planning. Add at most 250 stable `IMP-*` contracts with requirement links,\n+owned files/data/interfaces, dependencies, non-goals, platform distinctions,\n+verification, asset assessment, and canonical source links. Validate coverage,\n+unique IDs, ownership, and acyclic dependencies. Allocate only ready\n+unassigned contracts, using monotonic B/R counters and batches of no more than\n+seven R IDs; materialise at most ten corresponding B runbooks. Each B writer\n+must contain a context packet, output list, validation procedure,\n+checkpoint/update procedure, collision stop rule, and stop condition. Do not\n+create R-series files yourself.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Atomically update the JSON/Markdown ledger counters, chapter state, contract\n+allocations, and checkpoint after validation. Never renumber, replace, or\n+rewrite an accepted B/R contract. If work remains, create exactly one new\n+dispatcher with the next monotonic dispatcher ID and a later sequence. If no\n+queued chapter or ready contract remains, create exactly one final audit\n+B-series runbook that validates all completed catalogue expansions and batches;\n+it must not pretend to generate or review all work in this dispatch.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Validate JSON, the 250-contract chapter cap, no more than ten newly-created B\n+files, no more than seven assigned R IDs per B file, unique B/R/IMP IDs,\n+dependency closure, provenance values, asset metadata, output ownership, and\n+the successor/final-audit choice. Stop and report a source conflict, missing\n+coverage, cycle, ID/path collision, unresolved authority, or any need to\n+overwrite accepted work.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop immediately after one chapter expansion (or none), one allocation wave,\n+and exactly one successor dispatcher or final audit task. This is not a\n+recursive prompt and must not materialise a whole-game plan.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- This iteration expands at most one eligible chapter and adds no more than 250 IMP contracts.\n+- It creates at most ten bounded B-series authoring tasks, each with at most seven assigned R-series outputs.\n+- Every created B task has its context packet, output list, validation, checkpoint/update, collision protection, and stop condition.\n+- If queued or ready work remains, exactly one successor dispatcher is created; otherwise exactly one final audit B-series task is created.\n+- IDs, manifest ownership, provenance, asset assessments, and dependencies are validated without overwriting accepted work.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..5e24170a9f17243df4715c1ab64fdb1d57f52d9b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@\n+# Implementation-runbook authoring context\n+\n+This collection creates implementation instructions only. The canonical project\n+scope is [PROJECT_BRIEF.md](../PROJECT_BRIEF.md); read the canonical\n+[specification](../specification/README.md) and the allocation ledger at\n+[`../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`](../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json)\n+before writing an R-series file. Do not infer, approve, or implement unresolved\n+decisions. This collection is a child of the factory collection and its R-series\n+output is registered as its own child collection.\n+\n+The initial wave is deliberately limited to the already allocated SHARD-01\n+foundation contracts. Future work is created only by the dispatcher, one\n+catalogue chapter and at most ten B-series tasks at a time.\ndiff --git a/runbooks/.supervisor-children/mock-fantasy-quest-4.json b/runbooks/.supervisor-children/mock-fantasy-quest-4.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..06eefe3c3f6bfb75799bd665798dfd3c8424bb21\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/runbooks/.supervisor-children/mock-fantasy-quest-4.json\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\n+{\"runbooks_dir\":\"../projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks\"}\n\n exited 1 in 547ms:\nF.F....                            